WEBVTT

01:13.073 --> 01:15.936
BONASERA:
I believe in America.

01:16.036 --> 01:18.979
America has made my fortune.

01:19.079 --> 01:23.143
And I raised my daughter
in the American fashion.

01:23.243 --> 01:28.168
I gave her freedom,
but I taught her
never to dishonor her family.

01:29.569 --> 01:32.713
She found a boyfriend,
not an Italian.

01:32.813 --> 01:34.835
She went to the movies
with him.

01:34.935 --> 01:37.277
She stayed out late.

01:37.377 --> 01:40.000
I didn't protest.

01:40.100 --> 01:44.865
Two months ago
he took her for a drive
with another boyfriend.

01:45.786 --> 01:48.489
They made her drink whiskey

01:48.589 --> 01:52.933
and then they tried to
take advantage of her.

01:53.033 --> 01:57.197
She resisted,
she kept her honor.

01:58.439 --> 02:01.522
So they beat her
like an animal.

02:03.324 --> 02:08.349
When I went to the hospital,
her nose was broken,

02:08.449 --> 02:12.893
her jaw was shattered,
held together by wire.

02:15.016 --> 02:18.499
She couldn't even weep
because of the pain.

02:20.541 --> 02:24.025
But I wept.
Why did I weep?

02:26.707 --> 02:29.070
She was the light
of my life.

02:31.032 --> 02:33.034
Beautiful girl.

02:36.437 --> 02:39.240
Now she will never be
beautiful again.

02:43.124 --> 02:45.126
(COUGHS)

02:45.927 --> 02:47.929
Sorry.

02:55.617 --> 03:00.122
I went to the police,
like a good American.

03:00.222 --> 03:04.006
These two boys
were brought to trial.

03:04.106 --> 03:06.848
The judge sentenced them
to three years in prison,

03:06.948 --> 03:09.111
but suspended
the sentence.

03:10.272 --> 03:12.574
Suspended the sentence!

03:12.674 --> 03:15.397
They went free
that very day!

03:17.599 --> 03:20.863
I stood in the courtroom
like a fool.

03:20.963 --> 03:24.486
And those two bastards,
they smiled at me.

03:25.687 --> 03:27.069
Then I said to my wife,

03:27.169 --> 03:31.253
"For justice,
we must go to Don Corleone."

03:36.699 --> 03:38.040
VITO: Why did you
go to the police?

03:38.140 --> 03:40.302
Why didn't you
come to me first?

03:41.223 --> 03:42.765
What do you want of me?

03:42.865 --> 03:47.290
Tell me anything,
but do what I beg you to do.

03:47.390 --> 03:49.392
What is that?

04:00.163 --> 04:02.165
(WHISPERING)
I want them dead.

04:13.536 --> 04:15.538
That I cannot do.

04:16.779 --> 04:19.262
I'll give you
anything you ask.

04:21.584 --> 04:23.286
We've known each
other many years,

04:23.386 --> 04:28.091
but this is the first time
you ever came to me
for counsel, for help.

04:28.191 --> 04:30.534
I can't remember
the last time that

04:30.634 --> 04:34.377
you invited me to your house
for a cup of coffee.

04:34.477 --> 04:38.341
Even though my wife
is godmother to your
only child.

04:38.441 --> 04:40.343
But let's be frank here.

04:40.443 --> 04:43.347
You never wanted
my friendship.

04:43.447 --> 04:47.190
And you were afraid
to be in my debt.

04:47.290 --> 04:49.773
BONASERA:
I didn't want to
get into trouble.

04:50.974 --> 04:52.976
I understand.

04:54.017 --> 04:56.940
You found Paradise
in America.

04:59.102 --> 05:00.964
You had a good trade,
made a good living,

05:01.064 --> 05:03.887
Police protected you
and there were courts of law.

05:03.987 --> 05:05.989
You didn't need
a friend like me.

05:08.232 --> 05:11.816
But now you come
to me and you say,

05:11.916 --> 05:14.358
"Don Corleone,
give me justice."

05:16.240 --> 05:19.063
But you don't ask
with respect.

05:19.163 --> 05:25.549
You don't offer friendship.
You don't even think
to call me Godfather.

05:25.649 --> 05:29.073
Instead, you come
into my house on the day
my daughter is to be married

05:29.173 --> 05:32.517
and ask me to do
murder for money.

05:32.617 --> 05:35.119
BONASERA:
I ask you for justice.

05:35.219 --> 05:37.942
That is not justice.
Your daughter is still alive.

05:39.183 --> 05:42.747
Let them suffer, then,
as she suffers.

05:44.629 --> 05:46.631
How much shall I pay you?

05:53.117 --> 05:55.119
(CAT MEOWS)

06:01.766 --> 06:05.590
Bonasera, Bonasera.

06:05.690 --> 06:09.975
What have I ever done
to make you treat me
so disrespectfully?

06:11.056 --> 06:13.558
If you'd come to me
in friendship,

06:13.658 --> 06:19.124
then the scum that ruined
your daughter would be
suffering this very day.

06:19.224 --> 06:21.486
And if by chance,
an honest man like yourself

06:21.586 --> 06:24.389
should make enemies,
then they would become
my enemies.

06:27.312 --> 06:30.035
And then they
would fear you.

06:33.478 --> 06:35.480
Be my friend?

06:39.445 --> 06:41.447
Godfather?

06:45.691 --> 06:47.693
Good.

06:48.974 --> 06:51.197
Some day, and that day
may never come,

06:51.297 --> 06:54.139
I'll call upon you
to do a service for me.

06:55.461 --> 06:59.285
But, uh... until that day,

06:59.385 --> 07:03.689
accept this justice as a gift
on my daughter's wedding day.

07:03.789 --> 07:05.051
Grazie, Godfather.

07:05.151 --> 07:06.292
Prego.

07:06.392 --> 07:08.394
(PEOPLE CHATTERING OUTSIDE)

07:13.319 --> 07:16.002
Give this to Clemenza.

07:18.204 --> 07:21.828
I want reliable people
people that aren't going to be
carried away.

07:21.928 --> 07:27.193
We were not murderers,
in spite of what this
undertaker says.

07:27.293 --> 07:29.535
(BAND PLAYING
TRADITIONAL ITALIAN MUSIC)

07:35.261 --> 07:37.263
(PEOPLE CHATTERING)

07:51.318 --> 07:52.539
Where's Michael?

07:52.639 --> 07:55.742
Don't worry,
it's early.

07:55.842 --> 07:58.945
We're not taking the picture
without Michael.

07:59.045 --> 08:01.048
(SPEAKING ITALIAN)

08:05.292 --> 08:06.353
What's the matter?

08:06.453 --> 08:08.455
It's Michael.

08:40.568 --> 08:42.570
(ALL CHEERING)

08:57.465 --> 08:59.467
VITO: Don Barzini.

09:02.590 --> 09:04.592
(VITO SPEAKING ITALIAN)

09:15.563 --> 09:18.747
Hey, Paulie!
Let me have some wine.

09:18.847 --> 09:21.149
Paulie! More wine.

09:21.249 --> 09:22.831
Music plays.

09:22.931 --> 09:24.553
Ah, you look terrific
on the floor.

09:24.653 --> 09:26.354
What, you a dance
judge or something?

09:26.454 --> 09:28.116
(SPEAKING ITALIAN)

09:28.216 --> 09:29.478
Go take a walk around
the neighborhood.

09:29.578 --> 09:31.580
Do your job.

09:36.184 --> 09:38.126
(MUSIC STOPS)

09:38.226 --> 09:39.848
Hey, Sandra, come on,
do me a favor.
Watch the kids.

09:39.948 --> 09:41.450
Don't let them run wild,
all right?

09:41.550 --> 09:44.032
Well, you watch
yourself, all right?

09:45.273 --> 09:47.276
(BAND PLAYING MAZURKA)

10:05.334 --> 10:09.578
20, 30 grand.
In small bills, cash.

10:10.379 --> 10:12.762
In that little silk purse.

10:12.862 --> 10:16.485
If this were somebody
else's wedding...
Sfortunato!

10:16.585 --> 10:17.727
Hey, Paulie!

10:17.827 --> 10:21.651
I got two gabagool,
capocol, and a prosciut.

10:21.751 --> 10:23.753
PAULIE: Stupid jerk!

10:31.961 --> 10:33.963
Hey, what's the matter?

10:46.135 --> 10:47.477
Have to go back to work.

10:47.577 --> 10:49.479
Oh, Tom.
It's part of the wedding.

10:49.579 --> 10:53.062
No Sicilian can refuse
any request on his
daughter's wedding day.

10:56.546 --> 10:58.608
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

10:58.708 --> 11:03.913
Don Corleone, I am honored
and grateful that you have
invited me to your home.

11:06.556 --> 11:08.138
Hey!

11:08.238 --> 11:09.419
Partire. Get out of here!

11:09.519 --> 11:11.962
It's a private party.
Go on!

11:12.762 --> 11:13.904
What is it?

11:14.004 --> 11:16.046
Hey, it's my sister's wedding.

11:22.452 --> 11:25.295
SONNY: Goddamn FBI
don't respect nothing!

11:27.578 --> 11:31.702
Hey! Come here, come here,
come here, come here!

11:45.916 --> 11:50.461
...but towards the end,
he was paroled to help with
the American war effort,

11:50.561 --> 11:53.624
so for the last six months
he's been working in my
pastry shop.

11:53.724 --> 11:56.347
Nazorine, my friend,
What can I do for you?

11:56.447 --> 11:58.469
Now that
the war is over,

11:58.569 --> 12:02.633
this boy, Enzo,
they want to repatriate
him back to Italy.

12:02.733 --> 12:05.116
Godfather, I have a daughter.

12:05.216 --> 12:08.599
You see, she and Enzo...

12:08.699 --> 12:12.503
You want Enzo to stay
in this country, and you want
your daughter to be married.

12:14.465 --> 12:16.707
NAZORINE: You understand
everything.

12:17.588 --> 12:19.951
Mr. Hagen. Thank you.

12:23.034 --> 12:25.256
Wait till you see
the beautiful wedding cake
I made for your daughter!

12:25.356 --> 12:27.058
Oof, like this! (CHUCKLES)

12:27.158 --> 12:29.881
The bride and the groom
with the angel...

12:35.086 --> 12:36.828
Who should I give
this job to?

12:36.928 --> 12:39.671
Not to our paisan.

12:39.771 --> 12:44.896
Give it to a Jew Congressman
in another district.
Who else is on the list?

12:51.983 --> 12:53.605
Hey, Michael!

12:53.705 --> 12:55.707
(ALL GREETING)

13:13.285 --> 13:17.129
TOM: He's not on the list,
but Luca Brasi wants
to see you.

13:22.615 --> 13:25.037
Is this...
Is this necessary?

13:25.137 --> 13:28.360
He didn't expect to
be invited to the wedding,
so he wanted to thank you.

13:28.460 --> 13:30.963
All right.

13:31.063 --> 13:36.489
Don Corleone, I'm honored
and grateful that you have
invited me to your home

13:36.589 --> 13:39.372
on the wedding day
of your daughter.

13:39.472 --> 13:41.914
May their first child
be a masculine child.

13:43.115 --> 13:45.117
Michael...

13:46.319 --> 13:49.662
That man over there
is talking to himself.

13:49.762 --> 13:52.625
See that scary guy
over there?

13:52.725 --> 13:54.347
He's a very scary guy.

13:54.447 --> 13:56.149
Well, who is he?
What's his name?

13:56.249 --> 14:00.933
His name is Luca Brasi.
He helps my father
out sometimes.

14:02.695 --> 14:04.958
Oh, Michael, wait...
He's coming over here!

14:05.058 --> 14:07.240
Michael!
(EXCLAIMS)

14:07.340 --> 14:09.342
Hey!

14:09.983 --> 14:11.725
You look terrific!

14:11.825 --> 14:14.007
My brother Tom Hagen,
Miss Kay Adams.

14:14.107 --> 14:16.109
How do you do?
Nice to meet you.
How do you do, Tom?

14:16.870 --> 14:19.372
Your father's been
asking for you.

14:19.472 --> 14:20.453
Very nice to meet you.

14:20.553 --> 14:22.555
Nice to meet you.

14:23.877 --> 14:26.540
If he's your brother,
why does he have
a different name?

14:26.640 --> 14:28.902
Oh, back when my brother,
Sonny, was a kid,

14:29.002 --> 14:30.544
he found Tom Hagen
on the street.

14:30.644 --> 14:34.568
And he had no home, and so
my father took him in.

14:36.329 --> 14:38.332
And he's been with us
ever since.

14:39.493 --> 14:41.495
He's a good lawyer.

14:42.296 --> 14:44.558
Not a Sicilian.

14:44.658 --> 14:46.880
I think he's going
to be consigliere.

14:46.980 --> 14:48.001
What's that?

14:48.101 --> 14:49.843
That's a,

14:49.943 --> 14:53.747
like a counselor, an advisor.
Very important to the family.

14:54.788 --> 14:56.830
You like your lasagna?

15:01.195 --> 15:03.377
Don Corleone.

15:03.477 --> 15:06.100
I am honored and grateful

15:06.200 --> 15:10.264
that you have invited me
to your daughter's wedding.

15:10.364 --> 15:12.366
(PAPER RUSTLING)

15:15.049 --> 15:18.312
On the day of
your daughter's wedding.

15:18.412 --> 15:23.337
And I hope that their
first child will be
a masculine child.

15:24.699 --> 15:29.824
I pledge my
ever-ending loyalty.

15:31.826 --> 15:33.768
For your daughter's
bridal purse.

15:33.868 --> 15:37.051
Thank you, Luca.
My most valued friend.

15:37.151 --> 15:42.397
Don Corleone, I'm going
to leave you now,
because I know you're busy.

15:42.997 --> 15:44.999
Thank you.

16:26.962 --> 16:28.964
(ALL SINGING)

16:34.049 --> 16:36.372
Signora Corleone!

16:37.373 --> 16:40.436
No! No! No!

16:40.536 --> 16:42.538
(CHATTERING)

16:45.341 --> 16:47.343
(SPEAKING ITALIAN)

16:49.425 --> 16:51.427
(SINGING CHE LA LUNA)

17:45.602 --> 17:47.604
(ALL SINGING)

17:49.246 --> 17:54.471
Senator Cauley apologized
for not coming personally,
but said you'd understand.

17:54.571 --> 17:58.876
Also some of the judges.
They've all sent gifts.

17:58.976 --> 18:00.237
(TOASTING IN ITALIAN)

18:00.337 --> 18:01.919
(WOMEN SCREAMING)

18:02.019 --> 18:04.021
What is that outside?

18:12.309 --> 18:16.794
Johnny! Johnny! Johnny!

18:17.915 --> 18:19.917
I love you!

18:22.560 --> 18:24.562
(SCREAMING CONTINUES)

18:29.687 --> 18:31.949
He came all the way
from California to come
to the wedding.

18:32.049 --> 18:33.231
I told you he was
going to come!

18:33.331 --> 18:35.233
Been two years.
He's probably
in trouble again.

18:35.333 --> 18:37.715
He's a good godson.

18:37.815 --> 18:42.160
Johnny, Johnny!
(SPEAKS IN ITALIAN)
Sing a song!

18:42.260 --> 18:44.262
(ALL CHEERING)

18:58.156 --> 19:00.658
You never told me
you knew Johnny Fontane!

19:00.758 --> 19:02.260
Sure.
You want to meet him?

19:02.360 --> 19:04.743
Huh? Oh...
Great! Sure.

19:04.843 --> 19:07.185
My father helped him
with his career.

19:07.285 --> 19:08.707
He did?

19:08.807 --> 19:09.868
How?

19:09.968 --> 19:11.910
(JOHNNY SINGING
I HAVE BUT ONE HEART)

19:12.010 --> 19:14.392
Let's listen to this song.
No, Michael...

19:14.492 --> 19:19.457
(WOMEN SCREAMING)
♪♪ This heart I bring you

19:20.619 --> 19:24.963
♪♪ I have but one heart

19:25.063 --> 19:27.786
♪♪ To share with you

19:29.828 --> 19:33.792
♪♪ I have but one dream

19:34.633 --> 19:38.677
♪♪ That I can cling to

19:39.558 --> 19:44.103
♪♪ You are the one dream

19:44.203 --> 19:47.326
♪♪ I pray comes true

19:48.567 --> 19:50.709
Please, Michael. Tell me.

19:50.809 --> 19:54.273
♪♪ My, darling,
until I saw you ♪♪

19:54.373 --> 19:55.754
Well, when Johnny
was first starting out,

19:55.854 --> 19:59.238
he was signed to this
personal service contract

19:59.338 --> 20:02.201
with a big bandleader.

20:02.301 --> 20:04.403
And as his career
got better and better,

20:04.503 --> 20:07.486
he wanted to get out of it.

20:07.586 --> 20:10.289
Now, Johnny
is my father's godson.

20:10.389 --> 20:13.653
And my father went
to see this bandleader.

20:13.753 --> 20:17.456
And he offered him $10,000
to let Johnny go,

20:17.556 --> 20:20.420
but the bandleader
said no.

20:20.520 --> 20:22.582
So the next day

20:22.682 --> 20:26.205
my father went to see him,
only this time
with Luca Brasi.

20:27.887 --> 20:30.229
And within an hour,

20:30.329 --> 20:35.855
he signed a release
for a certified check
of $1,000.

20:37.537 --> 20:39.199
Well, how did he do that?

20:39.299 --> 20:41.301
My father made him an
offer he couldn't refuse.

20:42.942 --> 20:44.944
What was that?

20:45.265 --> 20:48.088
Luca Brasi held a gun
to his head,

20:48.188 --> 20:50.290
and my father assured him
that either his brain

20:50.390 --> 20:53.393
or his signature
would be on the contract.

20:58.478 --> 21:00.480
That's a true story.

21:01.561 --> 21:03.563
(SINGING IN ITALIAN)

21:11.531 --> 21:14.174
That's my family, Kay.
It's not me.

21:15.175 --> 21:17.177
(ALL APPLAUDING)

21:26.707 --> 21:28.709
MAMA CORLEONE: Beautiful!

21:31.472 --> 21:33.874
(INDISTINCT CHATTERING)

22:00.701 --> 22:02.804
I'll take care of it.

22:02.904 --> 22:04.726
Tom...

22:04.826 --> 22:06.167
I want you to find Santino.

22:06.267 --> 22:08.549
Tell him to come
to the office.

22:15.837 --> 22:17.739
How are you, Fredo?

22:17.839 --> 22:21.402
Fredo. My brother Fredo,
this is Kay Adams.

22:22.524 --> 22:24.846
Hi.
How are you doing?

22:26.768 --> 22:27.949
This is my brother Mike.

22:28.049 --> 22:31.273
Are you having
a good time?
Huh?

22:31.373 --> 22:33.955
Yeah. This is
your friend, huh?

22:34.055 --> 22:35.757
JOHNNY: I don't
know what to do.

22:35.857 --> 22:38.700
My voice is weak.
It's weak.

22:40.382 --> 22:44.086
Anyway, if I had this part
in the picture, you know,

22:44.186 --> 22:46.848
it puts me right back
up on top again.

22:46.948 --> 22:49.531
But this...

22:49.631 --> 22:52.294
This man out there.
He won't give it to me,
the head of the studio.

22:52.394 --> 22:53.375
What's his name?

22:53.475 --> 22:55.497
Woltz. Woltz, he...

22:55.597 --> 22:58.781
He won't give it to me,
and he says there's no chance.

22:58.881 --> 23:00.883
No chance.

23:04.166 --> 23:06.168
TOM: Sonny?

23:06.608 --> 23:08.390
Sonny?

23:08.490 --> 23:10.492
(BOTH MOANING)

23:12.294 --> 23:14.296
(KNOCK ON DOOR)

23:14.817 --> 23:16.759
TOM: Sonny?

23:16.859 --> 23:18.200
Sonny, are you in there?

23:18.300 --> 23:19.482
What?

23:19.582 --> 23:21.584
The old man wants you.

23:22.625 --> 23:24.627
All right, One minute.

23:26.108 --> 23:28.110
(BOTH MOANING)

23:28.831 --> 23:30.833
WOMAN: Oh, Sonny!

23:31.954 --> 23:33.956
(SINGING IN ITALIAN)

23:38.721 --> 23:43.786
JOHNNY: A month ago
he bought the movie rights
to this book, a best-seller.

23:43.886 --> 23:46.669
And the main character
is a guy just like me.

23:46.769 --> 23:48.511
Why, you know, I wouldn't
even have to act.

23:48.611 --> 23:50.994
Just be myself.

23:51.094 --> 23:54.157
Godfather, I don't know
what to do. I don't know
what to do.

23:54.257 --> 23:55.238
(SNIFFLES)

23:55.338 --> 23:57.400
You can act like a man!

23:57.500 --> 23:59.522
What's the matter with you?

23:59.622 --> 24:04.407
Is this how you turned out?
A Hollywood finocchio
that cries like a woman?

24:04.507 --> 24:07.971
(MIMICKING JOHNNY)
"What can I do?
What can I do?"

24:08.071 --> 24:09.733
What is that nonsense?

24:09.833 --> 24:11.835
Ridiculous.

24:16.079 --> 24:17.541
You spend time
with your family?

24:17.641 --> 24:19.182
Sure I do.

24:19.282 --> 24:21.104
Good.

24:21.204 --> 24:25.609
Because a man who doesn't
spend time with his family
can never be a real man.

24:31.254 --> 24:34.678
You look terrible.
I want you to eat.

24:34.778 --> 24:36.920
Want you to rest well,
and in a month from now

24:37.020 --> 24:40.084
this Hollywood big shot's
gonna give you what you want.

24:40.184 --> 24:43.327
It's too late,
they start shooting
in a week.

24:43.427 --> 24:46.510
I'm going to make him
an offer he can't refuse.

24:49.393 --> 24:54.358
Now, just go outside, enjoy
yourself, and forget about
all this nonsense.

24:56.881 --> 24:58.622
I want you to
leave it all to me.

24:58.722 --> 25:00.724
All right.

25:10.574 --> 25:12.577
(BAND PLAYING)

25:24.749 --> 25:27.612
What time does
my daughter leave
with the bridegroom?

25:27.712 --> 25:30.014
In a few minutes,
right after they cut the cake.

25:30.114 --> 25:33.698
Now your new son-in-law,
do we give him something
important?

25:33.798 --> 25:36.141
Never. Give him a living,

25:36.241 --> 25:39.064
but never discuss the family
business with him.

25:39.164 --> 25:40.385
What else?

25:40.485 --> 25:42.107
Virgil Sollozzo called.

25:42.207 --> 25:44.389
Now, we're gonna have
to give him a day
sometime next week.

25:44.489 --> 25:46.611
We'll discuss it when
you come back from
California.

25:48.013 --> 25:49.875
When am I going
to California?

25:49.975 --> 25:51.877
I want you to go tonight.

25:51.977 --> 25:56.581
I want you to talk to this
movie big shot and settle
this business for Johnny.

25:57.823 --> 25:58.884
Now if there's nothing else,

25:58.984 --> 26:02.107
I'd like to go to
my daughter's wedding.

26:04.269 --> 26:07.232
Carlo, we're going to
take the picture.

26:08.273 --> 26:10.055
MICHAEL: Wait a minute.

26:10.155 --> 26:12.437
KAY: No, Michael. Not me.

26:16.922 --> 26:19.845
Okay, that's it.
Just like that now.
Hold it!

26:23.088 --> 26:25.090
(BAND PLAYING WALTZ)

27:58.505 --> 28:00.507
(BELL RINGING)

28:02.389 --> 28:04.391
(ALL CHATTERING)

28:09.837 --> 28:11.619
MAN: You need
a little more heat
on that arc.

28:11.719 --> 28:13.020
All right, start talking.

28:13.120 --> 28:16.464
I was sent by a friend
of Johnny Fontane.

28:16.564 --> 28:20.348
This friend is my client.
He would give his undying
friendship to Mr. Woltz,

28:20.448 --> 28:23.271
if Mr. Woltz would
grant us a small favor.

28:23.371 --> 28:25.673
Woltz is listening.

28:25.773 --> 28:29.857
Give Johnny the part
in that new war film
you're starting next week.

28:31.138 --> 28:33.140
(CHUCKLES)

28:35.583 --> 28:40.568
And, uh... What favor
would your friend grant
Mr. Woltz?

28:40.668 --> 28:44.172
You're gonna have some
union problems, my client
could make them disappear.

28:44.272 --> 28:48.376
Also one of your top stars
has just moved from
marijuana to heroin.

28:48.476 --> 28:50.138
Are you trying to muscle me?
Absolutely not...

28:50.238 --> 28:52.781
Now, listen to me,
you smooth talking
son-of-a-bitch!

28:52.881 --> 28:55.463
Let me lay it on the line
for you and your boss,
whoever he is.

28:55.563 --> 28:57.505
Johnny Fontane
will never get
that movie!

28:57.605 --> 28:59.027
I don't care how many

28:59.127 --> 29:02.150
Dago Guinea wop
greaseball goombahs
come out of the woodwork!

29:02.250 --> 29:03.552
I'm German-Irish.

29:03.652 --> 29:06.034
Well, let me
tell you something,
my Kraut-Mick friend.

29:06.134 --> 29:09.117
I'm going to make so much
trouble for you!
You won't know what hit ya.

29:09.217 --> 29:10.759
Mr. Woltz. I'm a lawyer.
I have not threatened...

29:10.859 --> 29:14.082
I know almost every
big lawyer in New York.
Who the hell are you?

29:14.182 --> 29:17.726
I have a special practice.
I handle one client.

29:17.826 --> 29:19.828
Now you have my number,
I'll wait for your call.

29:21.470 --> 29:24.513
By the way, I admire
your pictures very much.

29:29.278 --> 29:31.280
Check him out.

29:53.302 --> 29:54.804
It's really beautiful.

29:54.904 --> 29:55.885
Look at this.

29:55.985 --> 29:58.007
It used to decorate
the palace of a king.

29:58.107 --> 30:00.449
Yeah. Very nice.

30:00.549 --> 30:02.932
WOLTZ: Why didn't you say
you work for Corleone, Tom?

30:03.032 --> 30:05.254
I thought you were some
cheap two-bit hustler

30:05.354 --> 30:07.296
Johnny was running in,
trying to bluff me.

30:07.396 --> 30:09.579
I don't like to use
his name until it's
really necessary.

30:09.679 --> 30:11.421
WOLTZ:
How's your drink, Tom?
Fine.

30:11.521 --> 30:14.303
Hey come on over here with me.
I wanna show you something
really beautiful.

30:14.403 --> 30:16.926
You do appreciate
beauty, don't you?

30:19.889 --> 30:22.872
There you are.
$600,000 on four hoofs.

30:22.972 --> 30:26.916
I'll bet Russian czars
never paid that kinda
dough for a single horse.

30:27.016 --> 30:30.500
Khartoum.

30:31.901 --> 30:34.524
I'm not going
to race him, though.

30:34.624 --> 30:36.626
I'm going to put
him out to stud.

30:38.027 --> 30:40.030
Thanks, Tony.
Welcome.

30:40.350 --> 30:43.333
Let's get something
to eat, huh?

30:43.433 --> 30:46.736
TOM: Corleone is
Johnny's godfather.

30:46.836 --> 30:51.181
To the Italian people
that's a very religious,
sacred, close relationship.

30:51.281 --> 30:52.622
WOLTZ: And I respect that.

30:52.722 --> 30:55.265
Just tell him, he should
ask me anything else.

30:55.365 --> 30:57.507
But this is one favor
I can't give him.

30:57.607 --> 31:00.150
Well, he never asks
a second favor when he's
been refused the first.

31:00.250 --> 31:01.271
Understood?

31:01.371 --> 31:03.233
You don't understand.

31:03.333 --> 31:07.317
Johnny Fontane never
gets that movie.

31:07.417 --> 31:11.161
That part is perfect for him.
It'll make him a big star.

31:11.261 --> 31:15.345
I'm going to run him
out of the business,
and let me tell you why.

31:17.227 --> 31:21.932
Johnny Fontane ruined one
of Woltz International's
most valuable proteges.

31:22.032 --> 31:24.375
For five years,
we had her under training.

31:24.475 --> 31:27.418
Singing lessons,
acting lessons,
dancing lessons.

31:27.518 --> 31:29.940
I spent hundreds of thousands
of dollars on her,

31:30.040 --> 31:32.143
I was gonna make
her a big star.

31:32.243 --> 31:34.986
And let me be
even more frank.

31:35.086 --> 31:37.388
Just to show you that
I'm not a hardhearted man.

31:37.488 --> 31:40.031
That it's not all
dollars and cents.

31:40.131 --> 31:43.754
She was beautiful.
She was young,
she was innocent!

31:43.854 --> 31:46.077
She's the greatest
piece of ass I've ever had

31:46.177 --> 31:49.200
and I've had them
all over the world.

31:49.300 --> 31:55.406
And then Johnny Fontane
comes along with his olive oil
voice and Guinea charm.

31:55.506 --> 31:58.409
And she runs off.

31:58.509 --> 32:02.654
She threw it all away
just to make me
look ridiculous!

32:02.754 --> 32:07.939
And a man in my position
can't afford to be made
to look ridiculous!

32:08.039 --> 32:10.382
Now you get
the hell out of here!

32:10.482 --> 32:12.584
If that goombah
tries any rough stuff,

32:12.684 --> 32:14.846
you tell him
I ain't no bandleader.

32:16.167 --> 32:19.871
Yeah, I heard that story.

32:19.971 --> 32:23.955
Thank you for the dinner
and a very pleasant evening.

32:24.055 --> 32:26.918
Maybe your car can
take me to the airport.

32:27.018 --> 32:30.622
Mr. Corleone is a man
who insists on hearing
bad news immediately.

33:58.591 --> 34:00.593
(WOLTZ SCREAMING)

34:08.602 --> 34:10.604
(SCREAMING CONTINUES)

34:23.297 --> 34:24.838
You're not too tired,
are you, Tom?

34:24.938 --> 34:27.201
Oh, no, I slept
on the plane.

34:27.301 --> 34:30.364
I have the
Sollozzo notes here.

34:30.464 --> 34:32.466
Now...

34:33.667 --> 34:37.211
Sollozzo is known
as The Turk.

34:37.311 --> 34:39.253
He's supposed to be
very good with a knife,

34:39.353 --> 34:43.778
but only in matters
of business with some sort
of reasonable complaint.

34:43.878 --> 34:47.101
Uh, his business is narcotics.

34:47.201 --> 34:50.544
He has fields in Turkey,
where they grow poppy.

34:50.644 --> 34:54.468
In Sicily he has plants
to process them into heroin.

34:54.568 --> 34:58.072
Now, he needs cash,
he needs protection
from the police.

34:58.172 --> 35:00.354
For which, he gives
a piece of the action.

35:00.454 --> 35:02.196
I couldn't find out how much.

35:02.296 --> 35:05.159
The Tattaglia family
is behind him here
in New York.

35:05.259 --> 35:07.542
Now, they have to be
in it for something.

35:08.823 --> 35:10.485
What about his
prison record?

35:10.585 --> 35:13.408
Two terms.
One in Italy, one here.

35:13.508 --> 35:16.251
He's known as
a top narcotics man.

35:16.351 --> 35:18.353
Santino,
what do you think?

35:19.634 --> 35:21.636
A lot of money
in that white powder.

35:23.358 --> 35:24.699
Tom?

35:24.799 --> 35:26.541
TOM: Well I say, Yes.

35:26.641 --> 35:28.943
There's more money potential
in narcotics than anything
else we're looking at.

35:29.043 --> 35:31.866
Now, if we don't get into it,
somebody else will.

35:31.966 --> 35:33.788
Maybe one of
the five families,
maybe all of them

35:33.888 --> 35:35.550
Now with the money they earn,

35:35.650 --> 35:38.313
they can buy more Police
and political power.

35:38.413 --> 35:40.555
Then they come after us.

35:40.655 --> 35:42.918
Now we have the unions,
we have the gambling,

35:43.018 --> 35:44.479
and they're the best
things to have,

35:44.579 --> 35:47.122
but narcotics is the thing
of the future.

35:47.222 --> 35:48.844
If we don't get a piece
of that action,

35:48.944 --> 35:50.005
we risk everything we have.

35:50.105 --> 35:52.788
I mean, not now,
but in 10 years from now.

35:56.912 --> 35:59.875
So? What's your answer
gonna be, Pop?

36:04.800 --> 36:07.162
There.
Don Corleone.

36:08.644 --> 36:11.867
I need a man who
has powerful friends.

36:11.967 --> 36:14.750
I need a million
dollars in cash.

36:14.850 --> 36:16.952
I need, Don Corleone,
those politicians

36:17.052 --> 36:20.696
you carry in your pocket,
like so many
nickels and dimes.

36:22.057 --> 36:24.180
What is the interest
for my family?

36:24.540 --> 36:26.202
30%.

36:26.302 --> 36:29.024
In the first year
your end should be three,
four million dollars.

36:30.306 --> 36:33.369
And then it would go up.

36:33.469 --> 36:35.831
And what is the interest
for the Tattaglia family?

36:38.995 --> 36:40.997
My compliments.

36:44.320 --> 36:46.883
I'll take care
of the Tattaglias,
out of my share.

36:47.924 --> 36:52.188
So I receive 30%
for finance,

36:52.288 --> 36:55.391
political influence and
legal protection, that's
what your telling me?

36:55.491 --> 36:57.493
That's right.

36:58.615 --> 37:02.639
Why do you come to me?
Why do I deserve
this generosity?

37:02.739 --> 37:08.124
If you consider
a million dollars
in cash just finance,

37:08.224 --> 37:10.346
te salud, Don Corleone.

37:20.677 --> 37:25.902
I said that I would see you,
because I heard that you
were a serious man,

37:26.002 --> 37:28.405
to be treated
with respect.

37:32.969 --> 37:36.253
But, I must say no to you.

37:37.494 --> 37:40.357
And I'll give you
my reasons.

37:40.457 --> 37:43.300
It's true, I have
a lot of friends
in politics.

37:44.501 --> 37:46.243
But they wouldn't be
friendly very long

37:46.343 --> 37:48.846
if they knew my business was
drugs instead of gambling,

37:48.946 --> 37:52.049
which they regard
as a harmless vice,

37:52.149 --> 37:54.652
but drugs
is a dirty business.
Oh, Don Corleone...

37:54.752 --> 37:59.777
It doesn't make any difference
to me what a man does
for a living, understand.

37:59.877 --> 38:03.260
But your business is...

38:03.360 --> 38:04.982
A little dangerous.

38:05.082 --> 38:07.825
If you're worried about
security for your million,

38:07.925 --> 38:09.587
the Tattaglias
will guarantee it.

38:09.687 --> 38:11.989
Are you telling me
the Tattaglias would
guarantee our investment...

38:12.089 --> 38:14.091
Wait a minute.

38:20.338 --> 38:25.002
I have a sentimental weakness
for my children, and I spoil
them, as you can see...

38:25.102 --> 38:27.165
They talk when
they should listen.

38:27.265 --> 38:28.646
But anyway...

38:28.746 --> 38:31.129
Signor Sollozzo,
my no is final.

38:31.229 --> 38:34.092
And I wish to congratulate
you on your new business.

38:34.192 --> 38:37.495
I know you'll do very well,
and good luck to you.

38:37.595 --> 38:42.560
Especially since your
interests don't conflict
with mine. Thank you.

39:03.301 --> 39:05.043
Santino.

39:05.143 --> 39:07.145
Come here.

39:09.267 --> 39:11.129
What's the matter with you?

39:11.229 --> 39:12.771
I think your
brain is going soft

39:12.871 --> 39:15.894
from all that comedy you're
playing with that young girl.

39:15.994 --> 39:19.238
Never tell anybody
outside the family
what you're thinking again.

39:21.400 --> 39:23.402
Go on.

39:26.805 --> 39:29.548
Tom, what...
What is this nonsense?

39:29.648 --> 39:32.992
It's from Johnny.
He's starring
in that new film.

39:33.092 --> 39:35.094
Huh.

39:35.494 --> 39:36.595
Take it away.

39:36.695 --> 39:38.697
Take it over there.

39:39.338 --> 39:41.340
And, uh...

39:41.780 --> 39:44.063
Tell Luca Brasi
to come in.

39:50.069 --> 39:53.412
I'm a little worried
about this Sollozzo fellow.

39:53.512 --> 39:56.235
I want you to find out
what he's got under
his fingernails, you know.

39:57.597 --> 40:01.260
Go to the Tattaglias.

40:01.360 --> 40:05.685
Make them think that
you're not too happy
with our family

40:07.046 --> 40:09.409
and find out
what you can.

40:15.495 --> 40:19.178
(HAVE YOURSELF
A MERRY LITTLE CHRISTMAS
PLAYING ON RADIO)

40:21.341 --> 40:25.024
♪♪ Let your heart be light

40:26.866 --> 40:30.170
I got something
for your mother
and for Sonny

40:30.270 --> 40:34.935
and a tie for Freddy,
and Tom Hagen
got the Reynolds pen.

40:35.035 --> 40:36.216
What do you want
for Christmas?

40:36.316 --> 40:38.318
Me? Oh...Just you.

40:42.042 --> 40:45.445
(ON RADIO)
♪♪ Make the Yule-tide gay

40:46.887 --> 40:53.053
♪♪ From now on our troubles
will be miles away

40:57.017 --> 41:01.722
♪♪ Here we are
as in olden days

41:01.822 --> 41:05.746
♪♪ Happy golden days of yore

41:07.388 --> 41:09.390
♪♪ Faithful friends... ♪♪

41:09.990 --> 41:11.932
VITO: Andiamo, Fredo.

41:12.032 --> 41:13.654
Tell Paulie to get the car.
We're going.

41:13.754 --> 41:15.456
FREDO: Okay, Pop.

41:15.556 --> 41:17.097
I'll have to get it
myself, Pa.

41:17.197 --> 41:19.440
Paulie called in
sick this morning.
Huh?

41:21.242 --> 41:24.525
Paulie's a good kid.
I don't mind
getting the car.

41:27.928 --> 41:29.970
Buon natale, Caro.
Grazie.

42:12.774 --> 42:16.278
Luca!
I'm Bruno Tattaglia.

42:16.378 --> 42:17.999
I know.

42:18.099 --> 42:22.144
(BOTH SPEAKING ITALIAN)

42:26.868 --> 42:28.290
You know who I am?

42:28.390 --> 42:30.392
(SPEAKING ITALIAN)

43:25.488 --> 43:27.490
(SPEAKING ITALIAN)

43:31.534 --> 43:33.536
(GRUNTING)

43:38.862 --> 43:40.864
(CHOKING)

43:42.705 --> 43:44.708
(GASPING)

44:07.090 --> 44:10.834
Tom! Tom Hagen.
Merry Christmas.

44:10.934 --> 44:13.997
Hey! I'm glad I ran into you.
I want to talk to you.

44:14.097 --> 44:16.039
Well, I haven't got time.

44:16.139 --> 44:20.844
Make time, Consigliere.
Get in the car.

44:20.944 --> 44:25.529
What are you worried about?
If I wanted to kill you,
you'd be dead already.

44:25.629 --> 44:27.211
Get in.

44:27.311 --> 44:29.313
(CAROLS PLAYING ON RADIO)

44:38.122 --> 44:40.544
Fredo, I'm going to
buy some fruit.

44:40.644 --> 44:42.646
Okay, Pop.

44:48.612 --> 44:51.455
Merry Christmas.
I want some fruit.

45:19.884 --> 45:21.886
(SCREAMING)

45:52.117 --> 45:54.119
(WHIMPERING)

46:02.488 --> 46:04.490
(SOBBING)

46:11.016 --> 46:13.018
(SHOUTING)

46:14.860 --> 46:16.862
(BELL TOLLING)

46:19.064 --> 46:21.287
Mike, Would you like me
better if I were a nun?

46:21.387 --> 46:23.389
Like in the story,
you know.

46:26.032 --> 46:27.573
No.

46:27.673 --> 46:30.016
Well then, would you
like me better if I were
Ingrid Bergman?

46:30.116 --> 46:32.118
Now, that's a thought.

46:34.000 --> 46:35.982
Michael.

46:36.082 --> 46:38.985
No, I wouldn't like you better
if you were Ingrid Bergman.

46:39.085 --> 46:41.087
Mike.
What's the matter?

46:57.303 --> 46:59.946
They don't say
if he's dead or alive.

47:07.274 --> 47:09.276
(HORN BLARING)

47:22.289 --> 47:23.710
Sonny, Michael.

47:23.810 --> 47:25.432
SONNY:
Michael, where you been?

47:25.532 --> 47:27.074
Is he all right?

47:27.174 --> 47:28.395
We don't know yet.

47:28.495 --> 47:31.238
There are all
kinds of stories.

47:31.338 --> 47:33.340
He was hit bad, Mikey.

47:34.381 --> 47:35.682
Are you there?

47:35.782 --> 47:37.805
Yeah, I'm here.

47:37.905 --> 47:40.007
Where have you been?
I was worried.

47:40.107 --> 47:42.369
Didn't Tom tell you
I called?

47:42.469 --> 47:44.652
No. Look, come home, kid.

47:44.752 --> 47:46.914
You should be with Mama,
you hear?
All right.

47:54.441 --> 47:56.444
SANDRA: Oh, my God.

47:57.805 --> 47:58.786
(CLATTERING)

47:58.886 --> 47:59.867
(GASPING)

47:59.967 --> 48:01.429
Sonny!

48:01.529 --> 48:03.531
(BABY CRYING)

48:07.895 --> 48:10.238
(KNOCK ON DOOR)

48:10.338 --> 48:12.600
Stay back there.

48:12.700 --> 48:15.383
Who is it?
Open up, it's Clemenza.

48:17.825 --> 48:21.009
There's more news
about your old man.

48:21.109 --> 48:22.971
Word is out
in the street that
he's already dead.

48:23.071 --> 48:25.173
What's the matter...
What's the matter
with you?

48:25.273 --> 48:27.495
Sonny, take it easy!
Take it easy!

48:27.595 --> 48:28.776
Where was Paulie?

48:28.876 --> 48:30.899
Paulie was out sick.
He's been sick all winter.

48:30.999 --> 48:32.060
How many times
he been sick?

48:32.160 --> 48:33.942
Only maybe three, four times.

48:34.042 --> 48:35.723
I mean, I asked Freddy if he
wants me to get a different
bodyguard. He said no.

48:35.804 --> 48:37.625
Pick him up now.
Do me a favour,
pick him up right now.

48:37.725 --> 48:39.467
I don't care how sick he is.
If he's breathing,

48:39.567 --> 48:42.110
I want you to bring him
to my father's house now,
you understand? Now.

48:42.210 --> 48:43.632
Yeah, You want me to
send any people over here?

48:43.732 --> 48:45.794
No, no, no.
Just you and him.
Go ahead.

48:45.894 --> 48:47.896
(BABY CRYING)

48:49.618 --> 48:51.620
(DOOR SHUTS)

48:52.621 --> 48:54.483
Okay, I'm...

48:54.583 --> 48:57.005
I'm going to have a couple
of our people come over to the
house. Couple of our people.

48:57.105 --> 48:59.107
(TELEPHONE RINGING)

49:01.510 --> 49:02.491
Hello?

49:02.591 --> 49:03.652
SOLLOZZO:
Santino Corleone?

49:03.752 --> 49:06.495
Yeah.
We have Tom Hagen.

49:06.595 --> 49:10.339
You got three hours
he'll be released
with our proposition.

49:10.439 --> 49:13.862
Listen to everything
he has to say before
you do anything.

49:13.962 --> 49:15.264
What's done is done.

49:15.364 --> 49:18.547
And don't lose that famous
temper of yours, eh, Sonny?

49:18.647 --> 49:20.269
I'll wait.

49:20.369 --> 49:22.371
(HANGS UP)

49:34.503 --> 49:36.505
SOLLOZZO:
Your boss is dead.

49:39.468 --> 49:41.771
I know you're not
in the muscle end
of the family, Tom,

49:41.871 --> 49:44.894
so I don't want
you to be scared.

49:44.994 --> 49:48.357
I want you to help
the Corleones and
I want you to help me.

49:52.762 --> 49:57.366
Yeah, we got him outside
his office just about an hour
after we picked you up.

49:58.848 --> 50:00.850
Drink it.

50:04.654 --> 50:07.977
So now, It's up to you
to make the peace between
me and Sonny.

50:12.502 --> 50:15.265
Sonny was hot for my deal,
wasn't he?

50:16.666 --> 50:18.668
And you knew it was
the right thing to do.

50:20.670 --> 50:23.733
Sonny will come after you
with everything he's got.

50:23.833 --> 50:25.835
That will be his
first reaction, sure.

50:27.037 --> 50:29.940
That's why you gotta talk
some sense into him.

50:30.040 --> 50:33.744
The Tattaglia family
is behind me with
all their people.

50:33.844 --> 50:36.026
The other New York families
will go along with anything

50:36.126 --> 50:38.909
that will prevent
the full-scale war.

50:39.009 --> 50:41.471
Let's face it, Tom
and all due respect,

50:41.571 --> 50:44.174
the Don, rest in peace,
was slipping.

50:47.177 --> 50:49.179
Ten years ago,
could I have gotten to him?

50:54.104 --> 50:55.326
Well, now he's dead.

50:55.426 --> 50:58.028
He's dead, Tom,
and nothing can
bring him back.

50:59.710 --> 51:01.972
So you gotta talk to Sonny,

51:02.072 --> 51:06.397
you gotta talk
to the Caporegimes, Tessio,
and that fat Clemenza.

51:10.601 --> 51:12.603
It's good business, Tom.

51:14.084 --> 51:19.370
I'll try. But even
Sonny won't be able
to call off Luca Brasi.

51:22.013 --> 51:24.015
Yeah, well...

51:25.576 --> 51:28.099
Let me worry about Luca.

51:33.304 --> 51:35.526
You just talk to Sonny.

51:35.626 --> 51:37.989
And the other two kids.

51:40.992 --> 51:42.814
I'll do my best.

51:42.914 --> 51:44.916
Good.

51:45.797 --> 51:48.640
Now you can go.

51:54.966 --> 51:57.509
I don't like violence, Tom.

51:57.609 --> 51:59.751
I'm a businessman.

51:59.851 --> 52:02.414
Blood is a big expense.

52:05.417 --> 52:07.939
(HORN HONKING)

52:23.395 --> 52:25.217
He's still alive.

52:25.317 --> 52:29.261
They hit him
with five shots,
and he's still alive!

52:29.361 --> 52:34.086
That's bad luck for me,
and bad luck for you
if you don't make that deal.

53:18.771 --> 53:20.793
Your mother is over
in the hospital
with your father.

53:20.893 --> 53:23.816
Looks like he's gonna
pull through. Thank God.

53:25.658 --> 53:27.921
It's a lot of
bad blood.

53:28.021 --> 53:32.205
Sollozzo, Philip Tattaglia,
Bruno Tattaglia, Ramon...

53:32.305 --> 53:33.486
MICHAEL: You gonna
kill all those guys?

53:33.586 --> 53:35.368
Hey, stay out of it, Mickey.
Do me a favour.

53:35.468 --> 53:38.211
TOM: Sollozzo's the key,
you get rid of him,
everything falls into line.

53:38.311 --> 53:42.576
What about Luca?
Sollozzo thinks
he can control him.

53:42.676 --> 53:46.500
I don't know if Luca sold out,
we're in a lot of trouble.
Believe me, lot of trouble.

53:46.600 --> 53:48.101
Has anyone been
in touch with Luca?

53:48.201 --> 53:50.263
Yeah, we've been
trying all night.
He might be shacked up.

53:50.363 --> 53:51.585
Hey, Mickey, do me a favor...

53:51.685 --> 53:54.327
TOM: Luca never
sleeps over with a broad.

53:56.410 --> 53:59.753
Well, Tom,
you're consigliere.

53:59.853 --> 54:02.716
What do we do
if the old man dies?
God forbid.

54:02.816 --> 54:05.919
If we lose the old man,

54:06.019 --> 54:09.002
we lose the political contacts
and half our strength.

54:09.102 --> 54:11.965
The other New York
families might wind up
supporting Sollozzo

54:12.065 --> 54:14.688
just to avoid a long,
destructive war.

54:14.788 --> 54:19.413
This is almost 1946.
Nobody wants
bloodshed anymore.

54:19.513 --> 54:21.515
If your father dies,

54:23.597 --> 54:25.219
you make the deal, Sonny.

54:25.319 --> 54:27.982
You know, that's easy
for you to say, Tom.
He's not your father.

54:28.082 --> 54:30.084
I was as much a son
to him, as you or Mike.

54:33.607 --> 54:34.789
(KNOCK ON DOOR)

54:34.889 --> 54:37.271
What is it?

54:37.371 --> 54:39.834
Hey, Paulie, I thought
I told you to stay put.

54:39.934 --> 54:41.275
Well, the guy
at the gates. They...

54:41.375 --> 54:43.157
They said they
got a package.
Yeah?

54:43.257 --> 54:45.379
Tessio, go see
what it is.

54:48.583 --> 54:49.644
You want me
to hang around?

54:49.744 --> 54:50.965
SONNY: Yeah, hang around.
You all right?

54:51.065 --> 54:52.607
Yeah, I'm fine.
Yeah?

54:52.707 --> 54:55.089
There's some food
in the house.
Are you hungry or anything?

54:55.189 --> 54:56.891
No, it's all right.

54:56.991 --> 54:57.952
How about a drink?
How about a little brandy?
It's good to sweat it out.

54:58.032 --> 54:59.093
All right, sure.
Go ahead.

54:59.193 --> 55:01.195
That might be
a good idea.
Yeah, right.

55:03.037 --> 55:05.140
I want you to take care
of that son-of-a-bitch,
right away.

55:05.240 --> 55:07.662
Paulie sold out
the old man. That stronz...

55:07.762 --> 55:09.144
I don't wanna
see him again.

55:09.244 --> 55:11.146
Make that the first
thing on your list.
Understand?

55:11.246 --> 55:12.387
Understood.

55:12.487 --> 55:13.828
Hey, Mickey, tomorrow,

55:13.928 --> 55:15.710
You get a couple
of guys, you go over
to Luca's apartment.

55:15.810 --> 55:17.392
Hang around,
wait for him to show up.

55:17.492 --> 55:20.936
Uh, maybe we shouldn't
get Mike mixed up in this
too directly.

55:23.218 --> 55:26.822
Listen, uh... Hanging around
the house on the phone would
be a big help, huh.

55:27.943 --> 55:29.945
Try Luca again.

55:38.754 --> 55:39.735
What's the hell is this?

55:39.835 --> 55:41.577
TESSIO: That's
a Sicilian message.

55:41.677 --> 55:44.159
It means Luca Brasi
sleeps with the fishes.

55:52.327 --> 55:54.329
(CHILDREN YELLING)

55:58.253 --> 56:00.396
I'm going now.
What time are you
gonna be home tonight?

56:00.496 --> 56:02.498
I don't know.
Probably late.

56:04.700 --> 56:06.562
WOMAN: Don't
forget the cannoli!

56:06.662 --> 56:08.664
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

56:10.546 --> 56:13.089
Rocco, sit on the other side.

56:13.189 --> 56:15.191
You block the
rear-view mirror.

56:16.552 --> 56:18.134
That Sonny's running wild.

56:18.234 --> 56:20.016
He thinking of going
to the mattresses already.

56:20.116 --> 56:22.899
We gotta find a spot
on the West Side.

56:22.999 --> 56:25.902
Try 309 West 43rd Street.

56:26.002 --> 56:28.424
You know any good spots
on the West Side?

56:28.524 --> 56:29.666
Yeah, I'll think about it.

56:29.766 --> 56:31.107
Well, think about it while
you're driving, will ya?

56:31.207 --> 56:33.429
I want to hit New York
sometime this month.

56:33.529 --> 56:35.531
And watch out for the kids
when you're backing out.

56:45.982 --> 56:48.925
CLEMENZA: Hey, Paulie,
I want you to go down
39th Street, Carlo Santos,

56:49.025 --> 56:52.008
pick up 18 mattresses
for the guys to sleep with,
you bring me the bill.

56:52.108 --> 56:53.490
PAULIE: Yeah, all right.

56:53.590 --> 56:55.332
CLEMENZA: Make sure
they're clean,

56:55.432 --> 56:57.974
because those guys are gonna
be stuck up in there for
a long time, you know.

56:58.074 --> 57:00.377
PAULIE: They're clean
and they told me,
they exterminate them.

57:00.477 --> 57:02.419
CLEMENZA: (CHUCKLING)
Exterminate?
That's a bad word to use.

57:02.519 --> 57:06.423
Exterminate! Look at this guy.
Watch out, so we don't
exterminate you!

57:06.523 --> 57:09.106
(CLEMENZA
CHATTERING IN ITALIAN)

57:09.206 --> 57:11.208
(BOTH LAUGHING)

57:13.170 --> 57:15.732
CLEMENZA:
Pull over, will you?
I've got to take a leak.

57:20.537 --> 57:22.539
(SHIP HORN BLOWING)

57:26.583 --> 57:28.585
(SEAGULLS CAWING)

57:41.999 --> 57:44.001
(GUNSHOTS)

57:53.371 --> 57:55.373
(CAR DOOR OPENING)

57:57.375 --> 58:00.858
Leave the gun.
Take the cannoli.

58:19.037 --> 58:21.960
CLEMENZA: Hey, Mike!
Hey, Mikey!

58:23.601 --> 58:25.603
Yeah.
You're wanted
on the telephone.

58:31.970 --> 58:34.212
Who is it?
Some girl.

58:38.256 --> 58:39.558
Hello. Kay?

58:39.658 --> 58:40.879
KAY: How's your father?

58:40.979 --> 58:42.981
He's good.
He's going to make it.

58:43.502 --> 58:45.364
I love you.

58:45.464 --> 58:46.445
Huh?

58:46.545 --> 58:48.547
I love you!

58:49.227 --> 58:50.208
Michael?

58:50.308 --> 58:51.690
Yeah, I know.

58:51.790 --> 58:53.292
Tell me you love me.

58:53.392 --> 58:54.813
I can't talk.

58:54.913 --> 58:56.915
Can't you say it?

58:57.716 --> 59:00.299
Yeah, I'll see
you tonight.

59:00.399 --> 59:03.462
Hey Mikey, why don't you tell
that nice girl you love her?

59:03.562 --> 59:08.107
I love you with all my heart.
If I don't see you again soon,
I'm going to die!

59:08.207 --> 59:09.388
(CLEMENZA CHUCKLING)

59:09.488 --> 59:11.150
Come over here, kid,
learn something.

59:11.250 --> 59:14.273
You never know,
you might have to cook
for 20 guys some day.

59:14.373 --> 59:18.117
You see, you start out
with a little bit of oil,
then you fry some garlic.

59:18.217 --> 59:21.200
Then you throw in
some tomatoes,
some tomato paste,

59:21.300 --> 59:23.763
you fry it and make sure
it doesn't stick.

59:23.863 --> 59:27.807
You get it to a boil,
you shove in all your
sausage and your meatballs.

59:27.907 --> 59:29.809
Huh?

59:29.909 --> 59:31.951
Add a little bit
of wine.

59:35.194 --> 59:38.337
And a little bit of sugar.

59:38.437 --> 59:39.659
And that's my trick.

59:39.759 --> 59:41.060
Why don't you cut the crap.

59:41.160 --> 59:43.983
I have more important things
for you to do. How's Paulie?

59:44.083 --> 59:46.085
Oh, Paulie.
Won't see him no more.

59:47.647 --> 59:48.868
Where are you going?

59:48.968 --> 59:50.109
To the city.

59:50.209 --> 59:51.471
Send some bodyguards
with him, all right?

59:51.571 --> 59:52.712
No, I'm just going
to the hospital...

59:52.812 --> 59:54.234
Nevermind, send
somebody with him.

59:54.334 --> 59:57.157
CLEMENZA: He'll be all right.
Sollozzo knows
he's a civilian.

59:57.257 --> 59:59.259
Be careful, huh?
Yes, sir.

01:00:02.382 --> 01:00:04.384
Send somebody
with him anyway.

01:00:15.315 --> 01:00:17.317
(ALL OF MY LIFE
PLAYING ON RADIO)

01:00:32.733 --> 01:00:34.715
I have to go.

01:00:34.815 --> 01:00:37.438
Can I go with you?

01:00:37.538 --> 01:00:41.922
No, Kay. There's gonna
be detectives there,
people from the press.

01:00:42.022 --> 01:00:44.144
Well, I'll wait
in the cab.

01:00:46.707 --> 01:00:49.350
I don't want you
to get involved.

01:00:52.112 --> 01:00:54.114
When will
I see you again?

01:01:00.681 --> 01:01:02.863
Go back to New Hampshire,

01:01:02.963 --> 01:01:04.965
and I'll call you
at your parents' house.

01:01:06.607 --> 01:01:08.609
When will I see you
again, Michael?

01:01:10.491 --> 01:01:12.493
I don't know.

01:01:27.028 --> 01:01:29.030
(DOOR CLOSES)

01:03:23.747 --> 01:03:25.208
What are you doing here?

01:03:25.308 --> 01:03:27.370
You're not supposed
to be here now.

01:03:27.470 --> 01:03:30.934
I'm Michael Corleone.
This is my father.

01:03:31.034 --> 01:03:33.376
There's nobody here.
What happened to the guards?

01:03:33.476 --> 01:03:35.819
Your father just had
too many visitors.

01:03:35.919 --> 01:03:38.862
They interfered
with hospital service.

01:03:38.962 --> 01:03:42.325
The police made them leave
about 10 minutes ago.

01:03:46.810 --> 01:03:50.774
Get me Long Beach
45620, please.

01:03:53.337 --> 01:03:55.659
Nurse. Wait a minute.
Stay here.

01:03:59.743 --> 01:04:01.765
Sonny, Michael.
I'm at the hospital.

01:04:01.865 --> 01:04:04.568
Listen, I got here late,
there's nobody here.
SONNY: What? Nobody?

01:04:04.668 --> 01:04:08.973
Nobody. No Tessio's men,
no detectives, nobody.
Papa's all alone.

01:04:09.073 --> 01:04:10.414
Don't panic.
I'll send somebody.

01:04:10.514 --> 01:04:12.516
I won't panic.

01:04:12.997 --> 01:04:16.100
I'm sorry,
but you will have
to leave.

01:04:16.200 --> 01:04:18.582
Uh...

01:04:18.682 --> 01:04:21.385
You and I are going to move
my father to another room.

01:04:21.485 --> 01:04:24.508
Now, can you disconnect
those tubes so we can
move the bed out?

01:04:24.608 --> 01:04:25.910
That's out of
the question!

01:04:26.010 --> 01:04:28.152
Do you know my father?

01:04:28.252 --> 01:04:30.234
Men are coming
here to kill him.

01:04:30.334 --> 01:04:32.597
Do you understand?

01:04:32.697 --> 01:04:34.699
Now, help me, please.

01:05:01.005 --> 01:05:03.007
(DOOR CLOSING)

01:05:03.408 --> 01:05:05.410
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

01:05:51.577 --> 01:05:52.558
Who are you?

01:05:52.658 --> 01:05:55.381
I am Enzo, the baker.

01:05:56.422 --> 01:05:57.603
Do you remember me?
Enzo.

01:05:57.703 --> 01:05:58.884
Yes, Enzo.

01:05:58.984 --> 01:06:01.687
You'd better go,
there's going to
be trouble.

01:06:01.787 --> 01:06:04.050
If there is trouble,
I'll stay here to help you.

01:06:04.150 --> 01:06:06.472
For your father.
For your father.

01:06:07.593 --> 01:06:10.616
All right. Listen.
Wait for me outside,

01:06:10.716 --> 01:06:12.378
in front of the hospital,
all right?

01:06:12.478 --> 01:06:14.520
I'll be out in a minute.
Go ahead.
Okay.

01:06:28.534 --> 01:06:32.298
Just lie here, Pop.
I'll take care of you now.

01:06:34.020 --> 01:06:36.302
I'm with you now.

01:06:37.744 --> 01:06:39.746
I'm with you.

01:07:14.701 --> 01:07:17.644
Get rid of these.
Come here.

01:07:17.744 --> 01:07:22.229
Put your hand in your pocket,
like you have a gun.
You'll be all right.

01:07:24.591 --> 01:07:26.593
(MICHAEL SIGHS)

01:07:27.795 --> 01:07:29.797
(WHISPERING)
You'll be okay.

01:07:40.528 --> 01:07:42.530
(CAR APPROACHING)

01:08:13.641 --> 01:08:15.643
You did good.

01:08:31.139 --> 01:08:33.141
(SIRENS WAILING)

01:08:46.755 --> 01:08:50.799
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

01:09:03.892 --> 01:09:05.754
I thought I got all you
Guinea hoods locked up!

01:09:05.854 --> 01:09:07.156
What the hell
are you doing here?

01:09:07.256 --> 01:09:09.879
What happened to the men
who were guarding my father?

01:09:09.979 --> 01:09:11.721
Why, you little punk!

01:09:11.821 --> 01:09:13.642
What the hell are you doing
telling me my business!

01:09:13.742 --> 01:09:15.765
I pulled them
guys offa here, eh.

01:09:15.865 --> 01:09:18.848
Now you get outta here
and stay away from
this hospital!

01:09:18.948 --> 01:09:21.871
I'm not moving until
you put some guys
around my father's room.

01:09:22.471 --> 01:09:24.453
Phil, take him in!

01:09:24.553 --> 01:09:26.015
The kid's clean, Captain.

01:09:26.115 --> 01:09:27.376
He's a war hero.
He's never been...

01:09:27.476 --> 01:09:29.959
God damn it.
I said take him in!

01:09:32.201 --> 01:09:34.644
What's The Turk paying you
to set up my father, Captain?

01:09:35.925 --> 01:09:38.348
Take a hold of him.
Stand him up.

01:09:38.448 --> 01:09:40.450
Stand him up straight.

01:09:41.250 --> 01:09:43.252
(GRUNTS)

01:09:44.534 --> 01:09:46.856
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

01:10:02.312 --> 01:10:04.534
I'm the attorney for
the Corleone family.

01:10:04.634 --> 01:10:08.058
These men are
rivate detectives hired
to protect Vito Corleone.

01:10:08.158 --> 01:10:10.540
They're licensed
to carry firearms.

01:10:10.640 --> 01:10:12.582
If you interfere, you'll have
to appear before the judge

01:10:12.682 --> 01:10:14.684
in the morning
and show cause.

01:10:15.205 --> 01:10:17.207
All right.
Let him go.

01:10:18.008 --> 01:10:20.010
Come on.

01:10:49.560 --> 01:10:51.502
What's with
all the new faces?

01:10:51.602 --> 01:10:53.424
We'll need
them now.

01:10:53.524 --> 01:10:56.427
After the hospital thing,
Sonny got mad.

01:10:56.527 --> 01:10:59.450
We hit Bruno Tattaglia
four o'clock this morning.

01:11:00.851 --> 01:11:02.853
Jesus Christ.

01:11:09.540 --> 01:11:11.542
Looks like
a fortress around here.

01:11:14.185 --> 01:11:16.447
Tamaduch! Hey...

01:11:16.547 --> 01:11:19.530
A 100 buttonmen
on the street
24 hours a day.

01:11:19.630 --> 01:11:22.674
That Turk shows one hair
on his ass, he's dead.

01:11:25.236 --> 01:11:27.318
Hey, Mike, come here.
Let me look at you.

01:11:31.362 --> 01:11:34.546
You look beautiful,
beautiful.
You're gorgeous.

01:11:34.646 --> 01:11:35.787
Hey, listen to this.

01:11:35.887 --> 01:11:37.549
The Turk, he wants to talk!

01:11:37.649 --> 01:11:40.151
You got to imagine the nerve
of the son-of-a-bitch, eh?

01:11:40.251 --> 01:11:42.113
Craps out last night.
He wants
a meeting today.

01:11:42.213 --> 01:11:43.315
What did he say?

01:11:43.415 --> 01:11:45.557
What did he say...
(BABBLING)

01:11:45.657 --> 01:11:47.919
He wants us to send Michael
to hear the proposition.

01:11:48.019 --> 01:11:50.922
And he promises that the deal
is too good to refuse.

01:11:51.022 --> 01:11:52.924
Eh?
What about Bruno Tattaglia?

01:11:53.024 --> 01:11:54.566
That's part
of the deal.

01:11:54.666 --> 01:11:56.768
Bruno cancels out
what they did
to my Father.

01:11:56.868 --> 01:11:58.490
Sonny, we ought to hear
what they have to say.

01:11:58.590 --> 01:12:02.254
No. No. No more!
Not this time,
Consigliere.

01:12:02.354 --> 01:12:05.858
No more meetings,
no more discussions,
no more or Sollozzo tricks.

01:12:05.958 --> 01:12:07.740
You give them one message.
I want Sollozzo,

01:12:07.840 --> 01:12:09.021
or then it's all out war,
we go to...

01:12:09.121 --> 01:12:10.542
The other families
won't sit still...

01:12:10.642 --> 01:12:12.144
They hand me
Sollozzo!

01:12:12.244 --> 01:12:14.667
I don't want to hear this!
This is business,
not personal!

01:12:14.767 --> 01:12:16.428
They shot my father...

01:12:16.528 --> 01:12:19.752
Even the shooting of
your father was business,
not personal, Sonny.

01:12:19.852 --> 01:12:21.834
Well, then business
will have to suffer,
all right?

01:12:21.934 --> 01:12:23.636
And listen,
do me a favor, Tom.

01:12:23.736 --> 01:12:25.518
No more advice
on how to patch things up.

01:12:25.618 --> 01:12:27.620
Just help me win,
please, all right?

01:12:32.745 --> 01:12:34.327
(SIGHS)

01:12:34.427 --> 01:12:36.729
I found out about this
Captain McCluskey,
who broke Mike's jaw.

01:12:36.829 --> 01:12:38.291
What about him?

01:12:38.391 --> 01:12:41.174
He's definitely
on Sollozzo's payroll,
and for big money.

01:12:41.274 --> 01:12:42.455
See?

01:12:42.555 --> 01:12:44.377
McCluskey has agreed
to be The Turk's bodyguard.

01:12:44.477 --> 01:12:46.379
What you have
to understand, Sonny,

01:12:46.479 --> 01:12:50.223
is that while Sollozzo
is being guarded like this,
he's invulnerable.

01:12:50.323 --> 01:12:53.946
Nobody has ever
gunned down a New York
police captain. Never.

01:12:54.046 --> 01:12:57.230
It would be disastrous.
All the five families
would come after you, Sonny.

01:12:57.330 --> 01:12:59.953
The Corleone family
would be outcasts!

01:13:00.053 --> 01:13:03.256
Even the old man's
political protection
would run for cover.

01:13:05.218 --> 01:13:09.142
So, do me a favor.
Take this into consideration.

01:13:11.424 --> 01:13:12.726
(SIGHS)

01:13:12.826 --> 01:13:14.828
All right, we'll wait.

01:13:20.193 --> 01:13:24.417
We can't wait.
We can't wait.

01:13:24.517 --> 01:13:26.299
I don't care
what Sollozzo says,
about a deal,

01:13:26.399 --> 01:13:28.622
he's going to kill Pop.
That's it.

01:13:28.722 --> 01:13:31.565
That's the key for him.
We've got to get Sollozzo.

01:13:32.446 --> 01:13:34.227
Mike is right.

01:13:34.327 --> 01:13:36.830
SONNY: Let me
ask you something.
I mean...

01:13:36.930 --> 01:13:39.713
What about
this McCluskey, eh?

01:13:39.813 --> 01:13:41.815
What do we do
with this cop here?

01:13:46.500 --> 01:13:48.542
They want to have
a meeting
with me, right?

01:13:50.424 --> 01:13:54.868
It will be me,
McCluskey and Sollozzo.

01:13:56.750 --> 01:13:58.752
Let's set the meeting.

01:14:00.915 --> 01:14:04.078
Get our informers
to find out where
it's going to be held.

01:14:06.480 --> 01:14:10.304
Now we insist
it's a public place.
A bar, a restaurant.

01:14:10.404 --> 01:14:14.128
Some place
where there's people,
so I feel safe.

01:14:16.891 --> 01:14:19.834
They're gonna search me
when I meet them, right?

01:14:19.934 --> 01:14:21.936
So I can't have
a weapon on me then.

01:14:25.620 --> 01:14:30.585
But if Clemenza can figure
way to have a weapon
planted there for me

01:14:35.590 --> 01:14:37.592
then I'll kill them both.

01:14:39.994 --> 01:14:41.996
(CLEMENZA CHUCKLING)

01:14:42.837 --> 01:14:44.459
(LAUGHING)

01:14:44.559 --> 01:14:46.561
(ALL LAUGHING)

01:14:48.443 --> 01:14:49.784
SONNY: Hey.

01:14:49.884 --> 01:14:51.586
What are you gonna do?

01:14:51.686 --> 01:14:54.629
Nice college boy, huh?
Didn't want to get mixed up
in the family business.

01:14:54.729 --> 01:14:56.191
Now you want to gun down
a police captain,

01:14:56.291 --> 01:14:58.313
why, because he slapped you
in the face a little bit, huh?

01:14:58.413 --> 01:15:00.836
What do you think,
this is the army where
you shoot them a mile away?

01:15:00.936 --> 01:15:02.397
You got to get
close like this,
bada bing!

01:15:02.497 --> 01:15:05.040
You blow their brains
all over your nice
Ivy League suit.

01:15:05.140 --> 01:15:08.163
Come here.
You're taking this
very personal.

01:15:08.263 --> 01:15:11.687
Tom, this is business,
and this man is taking it
very, very personal.

01:15:11.787 --> 01:15:13.789
Where does it say
you can't kill a cop?

01:15:14.429 --> 01:15:15.530
Come on, Mikey...

01:15:15.630 --> 01:15:17.613
Tom, wait a minute.
I'm talking about a cop

01:15:17.713 --> 01:15:19.174
that's mixed up in drugs.

01:15:19.274 --> 01:15:22.217
I'm talking about
a dishonest cop.

01:15:22.317 --> 01:15:26.742
A crooked cop who got
mixed up in the rackets and
got what was coming to him.

01:15:26.842 --> 01:15:30.225
That's a terrific story.
We have newspaper people
on the payroll,

01:15:30.325 --> 01:15:32.327
don't we, Tom?

01:15:32.888 --> 01:15:34.790
They might like
a story like that.

01:15:34.890 --> 01:15:36.892
They might.
They just might.

01:15:40.376 --> 01:15:43.899
It's not personal, Sonny.
It's strictly business.

01:15:47.102 --> 01:15:48.604
CLEMENZA: It's as cold
as they come.

01:15:48.704 --> 01:15:52.288
Impossible to trace,
so you don't worry
about prints, Mike.

01:15:52.388 --> 01:15:55.211
I put a special tape
on the trigger
and the butt.

01:15:55.311 --> 01:15:57.313
Here. Try it.

01:16:08.644 --> 01:16:10.646
What's the matter?
Is the trigger too tight?

01:16:13.810 --> 01:16:15.271
(CHUCKLING)
I don't know.
My ears!

01:16:15.371 --> 01:16:17.073
Yeah, I left it noisy.

01:16:17.173 --> 01:16:21.157
That way it scares
away any pain-in-the-ass
innocent bystanders away.

01:16:21.257 --> 01:16:23.379
All right.
You've shot them both.
Now what do you do?

01:16:26.182 --> 01:16:28.405
Sit down,
finish my dinner.

01:16:28.505 --> 01:16:30.166
Come on, kid.
Don't fool around.

01:16:30.266 --> 01:16:33.770
Just let your hand drop
to your side
and let the gun slip out.

01:16:33.870 --> 01:16:36.012
Everybody will still think
you've got it.

01:16:36.112 --> 01:16:38.295
They're gonna be staring
at your face, Mike,

01:16:38.395 --> 01:16:41.258
so walk out of the place
real fast, but you don't run.

01:16:41.358 --> 01:16:42.779
Don't look nobody
directly in the eye,

01:16:42.879 --> 01:16:44.741
but don't look away either.

01:16:44.841 --> 01:16:46.823
Hey, they're gonna be
scared stiff of you,
believe me,

01:16:46.923 --> 01:16:48.925
so don't worry
about nothing.

01:16:50.407 --> 01:16:52.189
You know, you're gonna
turn out all right.

01:16:52.289 --> 01:16:54.711
You'll take a long vacation,
nobody knows where,

01:16:54.811 --> 01:16:56.813
and we're gonna
catch the hell.

01:16:57.494 --> 01:16:59.276
How bad do you think
it's gonna be?

01:16:59.376 --> 01:17:01.358
Pretty goddamn bad.

01:17:01.458 --> 01:17:04.481
Probably all the other
families will line up
against us.

01:17:04.581 --> 01:17:07.524
But it's all right.
These things have to happen
every five years or so.

01:17:07.624 --> 01:17:08.686
Ten years...

01:17:08.786 --> 01:17:10.207
How else do you get rid
of the bad blood.

01:17:10.307 --> 01:17:12.850
Been 10 years
since the last one.

01:17:12.950 --> 01:17:14.692
You know,
you got to stop them
at the beginning.

01:17:14.792 --> 01:17:16.894
Like they should have
stopped Hitler in Munich.

01:17:16.994 --> 01:17:18.616
They should've never let him
get away with that.

01:17:18.716 --> 01:17:21.779
They were just asking
for big trouble.

01:17:21.879 --> 01:17:25.683
You know, Mike,
we was all proud of you.
Being a hero and all.

01:17:26.484 --> 01:17:28.486
Your father too.

01:17:37.375 --> 01:17:39.377
(CLICKS)

01:17:55.913 --> 01:17:57.916
(SIGHS)

01:18:06.244 --> 01:18:10.548
Nothing. Not a hint.
Absolutely nothing.

01:18:10.648 --> 01:18:13.491
Even Sollozzo's people
don't know where
the meeting's gonna be held.

01:18:14.973 --> 01:18:18.076
How much time
do we have?

01:18:18.176 --> 01:18:20.799
They're going to pick you up
in front of Jack Dempsey's
joint in an hour and a half.

01:18:20.899 --> 01:18:23.882
Exactly an hour and a half.

01:18:23.982 --> 01:18:26.805
CLEMENZA: We could
put a tail on them.
See how that turns out.

01:18:26.905 --> 01:18:28.907
Sollozzo would
lose our ass going
around the block.

01:18:30.268 --> 01:18:31.970
What about
the negotiator?

01:18:32.070 --> 01:18:34.813
He's over at my place
playing pinochle
with a couple of my men.

01:18:34.913 --> 01:18:37.176
He's happy.
They're letting him win.

01:18:37.276 --> 01:18:39.818
It's too much of a risk
for Mike. Maybe we ought
to call if off, Sonny.

01:18:39.918 --> 01:18:43.462
The negotiator keeps on
playing cards until Mike
comes back safe and sound.

01:18:43.562 --> 01:18:45.864
So why doesn't he just blast
whoever is in the goddamn car.

01:18:45.964 --> 01:18:47.546
CLEMENZA:
It's dangerous.
They'll be looking for that.

01:18:47.646 --> 01:18:49.908
Sollozzo might not
even be
in the car, Sonny!

01:18:50.008 --> 01:18:51.030
(TELEPHONE RINGING)

01:18:51.130 --> 01:18:53.132
I'll get it.

01:19:02.942 --> 01:19:06.425
Yeah.

01:19:07.226 --> 01:19:09.228
Okay.

01:19:17.957 --> 01:19:20.139
Louis' restaurant
in the Bronx.

01:19:20.239 --> 01:19:21.461
Well, is it reliable?

01:19:21.561 --> 01:19:23.583
That's my man in
McCluskey's precinct.

01:19:23.683 --> 01:19:26.065
A police captain
has got to be on call
24 hours a day.

01:19:26.165 --> 01:19:28.568
He signed out at that number
between eight and ten.

01:19:29.449 --> 01:19:30.510
Anybody know this joint?

01:19:30.610 --> 01:19:34.314
Yeah, sure, I do.
It's perfect for us.

01:19:34.414 --> 01:19:36.476
A small family place,
good food.

01:19:36.576 --> 01:19:40.039
Everyone minds
his business. It's perfect.

01:19:40.139 --> 01:19:42.162
They've got
an old-fashioned toilet.

01:19:42.262 --> 01:19:45.545
You know, the box
and the chain thing.

01:19:47.227 --> 01:19:50.250
We might be able to
tape the gun behind it.

01:19:50.350 --> 01:19:54.454
All right. Mike,
you go to the restaurant,

01:19:54.554 --> 01:19:58.538
you eat, you talk
for a while, you relax.
You make them relax.

01:19:58.638 --> 01:20:00.300
Then you get up
and you go to take a leak.

01:20:00.400 --> 01:20:04.024
No, better still,
you ask for permission to go.

01:20:04.124 --> 01:20:05.585
Then you come back,
you come out blasting.

01:20:05.685 --> 01:20:08.789
And don't take any chances.
Two shots in the head apiece.

01:20:08.889 --> 01:20:10.390
Now listen.

01:20:10.490 --> 01:20:12.793
I want somebody good,
and I mean very good
to plant that gun.

01:20:12.893 --> 01:20:14.394
I don't want my brother
coming out of the toilet

01:20:14.494 --> 01:20:16.356
with just his dick
in his hands, all right?

01:20:16.456 --> 01:20:18.158
The gun will be there.

01:20:18.258 --> 01:20:21.181
All right, listen.
You drive him and you pick
him up after the job is done.

01:20:22.142 --> 01:20:24.144
Come on.
Let's move.

01:20:29.309 --> 01:20:32.413
Did he tell you
to drop the gun
right away?

01:20:32.513 --> 01:20:34.515
Yeah, a million times.

01:20:39.159 --> 01:20:40.821
You don't forget.

01:20:40.921 --> 01:20:43.584
Two shots apiece in the head
as soon as you come out
the door, all right?

01:20:43.684 --> 01:20:45.686
Let's go.

01:20:49.850 --> 01:20:52.133
How long do you think
it will be
before I can come back?

01:20:54.375 --> 01:20:56.517
At least a year, Mike.

01:20:56.617 --> 01:20:58.359
Listen,
I'll square it with Mom,

01:20:58.459 --> 01:21:00.982
that you're not seeing her
before you leave and...

01:21:02.784 --> 01:21:04.605
I'll get a message
to that girlfriend

01:21:04.705 --> 01:21:06.708
when I think
the time is right.

01:21:12.914 --> 01:21:14.916
Take care, huh?

01:21:16.958 --> 01:21:18.960
Take care, Mike.

01:21:51.433 --> 01:21:53.495
I'm glad you came, Mike.

01:21:53.595 --> 01:21:56.298
I hope we can
straighten everything out.

01:21:56.398 --> 01:21:59.742
I mean, this is terrible.
It's not the way
I wanted things to go at all.

01:21:59.842 --> 01:22:01.583
It should never
have happened.

01:22:01.683 --> 01:22:03.465
I want to straighten
everything out tonight.

01:22:03.565 --> 01:22:05.908
I don't want my father
bothered anymore.

01:22:06.008 --> 01:22:10.192
He won't be, Mike.
I swear on my children
that he won't be.

01:22:10.292 --> 01:22:13.636
But you got to keep
an open mind
when we talk.

01:22:13.736 --> 01:22:16.158
I mean, I hope
you're not a hothead
like your brother Sonny.

01:22:16.258 --> 01:22:18.120
You can't talk
business with him.

01:22:18.220 --> 01:22:19.482
(SPEAKING ITALIAN)

01:22:19.582 --> 01:22:21.444
McCLUSKEY:
Nah, he's a good kid.

01:22:21.544 --> 01:22:23.546
(SIGHS)

01:22:25.708 --> 01:22:29.091
I'm sorry about
the other night, Mike.

01:22:29.191 --> 01:22:33.316
Now, I've got to frisk you,
so turn around, huh?
On your knees, facing me.

01:22:38.000 --> 01:22:40.803
(SIGHS) I guess I'm getting
too old for my job.

01:22:41.804 --> 01:22:44.227
Too grouchy. (CHUCKLES)

01:22:44.327 --> 01:22:48.011
Can't stand
the aggravation.
You know how it is.

01:22:48.411 --> 01:22:50.393
(SIGHS)

01:22:50.493 --> 01:22:52.495
He's clean.

01:23:18.762 --> 01:23:20.764
Going to Jersey?

01:23:23.326 --> 01:23:25.328
Maybe.

01:23:35.739 --> 01:23:37.741
(TIRES SCREECHES)

01:23:41.425 --> 01:23:43.427
(HORNS BLARING)

01:23:50.194 --> 01:23:52.196
Nice work, Lou.

01:24:29.193 --> 01:24:31.296
How's the Italian food
in this restaurant?

01:24:31.396 --> 01:24:34.739
Good. Try the veal.
It's the best in the city.

01:24:34.839 --> 01:24:36.841
McCLUSKEY: I'll have it.

01:24:37.642 --> 01:24:39.644
(SPEAKING ITALIAN)

01:24:52.457 --> 01:24:54.459
(CORK POPS)

01:25:07.993 --> 01:25:09.995
(SIGHS)

01:25:11.997 --> 01:25:14.019
I'm going to speak
Italian to Mike.

01:25:14.119 --> 01:25:16.121
Go ahead.

01:25:21.647 --> 01:25:23.649
(SPEAKING ITALIAN)

01:26:34.801 --> 01:26:36.803
What I want...

01:26:37.524 --> 01:26:39.526
What's most
important to me,

01:26:42.449 --> 01:26:44.391
is that I have a guarantee.

01:26:44.491 --> 01:26:46.553
No more attempts
on my father's life.

01:26:46.653 --> 01:26:49.756
What guarantees
can I give you, Mike?

01:26:49.856 --> 01:26:51.318
I'm the hunted one!

01:26:51.418 --> 01:26:54.541
I missed my chance.
You think
too much of me, kid.

01:26:55.222 --> 01:26:57.224
I'm not that clever.

01:26:58.545 --> 01:27:00.627
All I want is a truce.

01:27:07.394 --> 01:27:09.396
I have to go
to the bathroom.

01:27:09.797 --> 01:27:11.799
Is it all right?

01:27:12.640 --> 01:27:14.642
When you got to go,
you got to go.

01:27:20.608 --> 01:27:22.550
I frisked him.
He's clean.

01:27:22.650 --> 01:27:24.652
Don't take too long.

01:27:27.855 --> 01:27:29.857
I've frisked
a thousand young punks.

01:28:05.854 --> 01:28:07.856
(TOILET FLUSHING)

01:28:45.654 --> 01:28:47.656
(SOLLOZZO SPEAKING ITALIAN)

01:29:10.680 --> 01:29:12.682
(TRAIN SCREECHING)

01:29:21.771 --> 01:29:23.773
(CHOKING)

01:30:22.833 --> 01:30:24.835
(PIANO MUSIC PLAYING)

01:31:04.716 --> 01:31:07.078
(SIREN WAILING)

01:31:19.050 --> 01:31:21.052
(INDISTINCT CHATTERING)

01:31:35.627 --> 01:31:37.629
(CAR ENGINE STARTS)

01:32:00.092 --> 01:32:02.094
(SIREN WAILING)

01:32:15.027 --> 01:32:17.029
(BABY CRYING)

01:32:20.473 --> 01:32:22.475
Okay, you take over.

01:32:25.198 --> 01:32:27.200
(ALL CHATTERING)

01:32:39.692 --> 01:32:40.793
I love you, Grandpa.

01:32:40.893 --> 01:32:42.896
(BABY CRYING)

01:32:44.177 --> 01:32:46.239
CONNIE: I'm sorry, Pa.
He doesn't know you yet.

01:32:46.339 --> 01:32:48.201
All right.

01:32:48.301 --> 01:32:50.243
Hey, big guy.
Give it to Grandpa.

01:32:50.343 --> 01:32:52.405
Okay.

01:32:52.505 --> 01:32:57.731
"I hope you get well, Grandpa,
and wish I would see you soon.
Love, your grandson Frank."

01:32:57.831 --> 01:32:59.953
Oh, thank you.

01:33:00.794 --> 01:33:02.896
Go with your mother.

01:33:02.996 --> 01:33:05.078
Go on. Take them
downstairs. Go on.
Come on, downstairs. Come on.

01:33:11.404 --> 01:33:13.407
Go on, Carlo,
you too.

01:33:15.208 --> 01:33:17.210
Go on.

01:33:20.213 --> 01:33:22.215
(ALL CHATTERING)

01:33:37.471 --> 01:33:39.293
What's the matter
with you, Carlo?

01:33:39.393 --> 01:33:41.395
Shut up
and set the table.

01:33:54.408 --> 01:33:56.410
(SIGHS)

01:33:56.931 --> 01:33:59.433
Since McCluskey's killing,

01:33:59.533 --> 01:34:03.057
the police have been
cracking down
on most our operations.

01:34:04.779 --> 01:34:06.781
And also the other families.

01:34:07.622 --> 01:34:09.804
There's been
a lot of bad blood.

01:34:09.904 --> 01:34:13.928
They hit us,
so we hit them back.

01:34:14.028 --> 01:34:16.251
Through our contacts
in the newspapers

01:34:16.351 --> 01:34:18.573
we've been able to put out
a lot of material

01:34:18.673 --> 01:34:21.876
about McCluskey being
linked with Sollozzo
in the drug rackets.

01:34:23.037 --> 01:34:25.039
See, things are starting
to loosen up.

01:34:26.401 --> 01:34:31.106
And I'm sending Fredo
to Las Vegas,

01:34:31.206 --> 01:34:33.828
under the protection
of Don Francesco of L.A.

01:34:33.928 --> 01:34:35.550
I want him to rest.

01:34:35.650 --> 01:34:38.693
I'm going to learn
the casino business. Yeah.

01:34:46.741 --> 01:34:48.743
(SOFTLY) Where's Michael?

01:35:00.796 --> 01:35:03.438
It was Michael
who killed Sollozzo.

01:35:05.721 --> 01:35:09.044
But he's safe.
We're starting to work
to bring him back.

01:35:30.946 --> 01:35:33.329
I want you to find out
where that old pimp
Tattaglia is hiding.

01:35:33.429 --> 01:35:35.331
I want his ass now.
Right now!

01:35:35.431 --> 01:35:38.935
Hey, Sonny,
things are starting
to loosen up a little bit.

01:35:39.035 --> 01:35:41.898
If you go after Tattaglia,
all hell's gonna break loose.

01:35:41.998 --> 01:35:43.740
Let the smoke clear.
Pop can negotiate.

01:35:43.840 --> 01:35:46.102
No. Pop can't so nothing
until he's better.
I'm gonna decide...

01:35:46.202 --> 01:35:48.544
All right. But your
war's costing us
a lot of money.

01:35:48.644 --> 01:35:50.386
Nohting's coming in.
We can't do business.

01:35:50.486 --> 01:35:52.789
Well, neither can they.
Don't worry about it.
We don't have it over here.

01:35:52.889 --> 01:35:53.870
We can't afford
a stalemate.

01:35:53.970 --> 01:35:55.111
Well, there ain't
no more stalemate.

01:35:55.211 --> 01:35:56.873
I'm gonna end it
by killing that old bastard!

01:35:56.973 --> 01:35:59.035
Yeah, you're getting
a great reputation!
I hope you're enjoying it!

01:35:59.135 --> 01:36:00.677
You just do
what I tell you to do!

01:36:00.777 --> 01:36:03.359
God damn it!
If I had a wartime
consigliere, a Sicilian,

01:36:03.459 --> 01:36:05.081
I wouldn't be in this shape!

01:36:05.181 --> 01:36:07.183
Pop had Genco.
Look what I got.

01:36:08.865 --> 01:36:10.847
(SIGHS)

01:36:10.947 --> 01:36:12.949
I'm sorry.
I didn't mean that.

01:36:14.511 --> 01:36:16.513
Ma made a little dinner.
It's Sunday.

01:36:18.435 --> 01:36:19.776
You know, niggers
are having a good time

01:36:19.876 --> 01:36:22.739
with our policy banks
up there in Harlem.

01:36:22.839 --> 01:36:27.024
Driving them new Cadillacs,
paying 50% on a bet.

01:36:27.124 --> 01:36:30.387
I knew this was going
to happen when they
started making big money.

01:36:30.487 --> 01:36:33.670
Papa never talked
business at the table
in front of the kids.

01:36:33.770 --> 01:36:35.192
CARLO: Hey,
shut up, Connie...

01:36:35.292 --> 01:36:37.814
Don't you ever
tell her to shut up.
You got that?

01:36:38.535 --> 01:36:40.537
Don't interfere.

01:36:41.939 --> 01:36:44.401
You know, Sonny, Tom,
I'd like to talk to you
maybe after dinner.

01:36:44.501 --> 01:36:45.843
I could doing a lot more
for the family...

01:36:45.943 --> 01:36:47.945
We don't discuss
business at the table.

01:37:17.495 --> 01:37:19.497
(WHISTLES)

01:37:27.345 --> 01:37:29.347
(HORN HONKS)

01:37:35.633 --> 01:37:37.635
(IN ITALIAN)

01:37:43.201 --> 01:37:45.203
(SPEAKS ITALIAN)

01:38:10.389 --> 01:38:12.391
Grazie.

01:38:14.272 --> 01:38:15.574
(IN ENGLISH)
To Corleone.

01:38:15.674 --> 01:38:17.676
(IN ITALIAN)

01:38:40.139 --> 01:38:42.141
(BELL TOLLING)

01:38:45.704 --> 01:38:47.867
Michael. Corleone.

01:38:59.679 --> 01:39:01.681
(BOTH SPEAK ITALIAN)

01:39:25.105 --> 01:39:29.209
(IN ENGLISH)
Hey, hey, take me
to the America, G.I.!

01:39:29.309 --> 01:39:33.573
Hey, hey, take me
to the America, G.I.!
Clark Gable! Hey!

01:39:33.673 --> 01:39:37.217
America! America! Take me
to the America, G.I.!

01:39:37.317 --> 01:39:39.219
Clark Gable, Rita Hayworth!

01:39:39.319 --> 01:39:41.321
(GRUMBLING IN ITALIAN)

01:39:42.682 --> 01:39:44.684
(WOMEN SINGING)

01:39:56.056 --> 01:39:58.058
(MEN SPEAKING ITALIAN)

01:39:59.540 --> 01:40:01.542
(SPEAKING ITALIAN)

01:40:31.692 --> 01:40:33.694
(SPEAKING ITALIAN)

01:41:02.524 --> 01:41:04.526
(REPEATING IN ITALIAN)

01:41:10.652 --> 01:41:11.913
Eh, Calo?

01:41:12.013 --> 01:41:14.015
(REPEATING IN ITALIAN)

01:41:33.675 --> 01:41:35.677
(REPEATING)

01:41:38.921 --> 01:41:40.923
No!

01:41:48.330 --> 01:41:50.572
(OWNER SHOUTING IN ITALIAN)

01:42:17.520 --> 01:42:19.642
(MEN CHATTERING IN ITALIAN)

01:42:33.296 --> 01:42:35.078
(IN ENGLISH)
I apologize
if I offended you.

01:42:35.178 --> 01:42:36.279
(TRANSLATING IN ITALIAN)

01:42:36.379 --> 01:42:38.381
I'm a stranger
in this country.

01:42:39.662 --> 01:42:41.865
And I meant no disrespect
to you or your daughter.

01:42:48.271 --> 01:42:50.273
I'm an American,
hiding in Sicily.

01:42:52.395 --> 01:42:54.397
My name is
Michael Corleone.

01:42:56.920 --> 01:42:59.202
There are people
who'd pay a lot of money
for that information.

01:43:03.246 --> 01:43:05.248
But then your daughter
would lose a father...

01:43:07.691 --> 01:43:09.693
Instead of
gaining a husband.

01:43:18.182 --> 01:43:20.184
I want to
meet your daughter.

01:43:21.265 --> 01:43:24.948
With your permission,
and under the supervision
of your family.

01:43:26.430 --> 01:43:28.432
With all respect.

01:43:43.047 --> 01:43:45.049
(IN ITALIAN)

01:43:46.651 --> 01:43:48.653
Apollonia.

01:44:16.361 --> 01:44:18.363
(VITELLI SPEAKING IN ITALIAN)

01:45:06.051 --> 01:45:08.053
(SPEAKING ITALIAN)

01:45:16.462 --> 01:45:18.464
(BELL TOLLING)

01:45:20.266 --> 01:45:22.268
(CHATTERING IN ITALIAN)

01:46:00.827 --> 01:46:02.829
(WOMEN CHATTERING)

01:46:15.202 --> 01:46:17.204
(COIN CLINKING)

01:46:40.547 --> 01:46:42.549
SONNY: I'm gonna
knock you dizzy.

01:46:48.315 --> 01:46:50.317
Save it for the library.

01:46:54.121 --> 01:46:56.203
Come on. We've got
to go pick up
my sister. Let's go.

01:47:14.782 --> 01:47:16.784
What's the matter?

01:47:17.185 --> 01:47:19.007
Huh?

01:47:19.107 --> 01:47:21.109
What's the matter?

01:47:22.470 --> 01:47:24.452
It was my fault!
Where is he?

01:47:24.552 --> 01:47:26.254
Sonny, please.
It was my fault.

01:47:26.354 --> 01:47:27.896
Sonny, it was my fault.
I hit him.

01:47:27.996 --> 01:47:29.938
I started a fight with him.
Please, Sonny.

01:47:30.038 --> 01:47:31.699
I hit him, so he hit me...

01:47:31.799 --> 01:47:33.802
(SHUSHING)

01:47:36.204 --> 01:47:40.028
Okay. I'm just going
to get a doctor to come
take a look at you.

01:47:40.128 --> 01:47:43.091
Sonny, please don't
do anything. Please
don't do anything.

01:47:44.613 --> 01:47:46.675
What's the matter with you?
What am I going to do?

01:47:46.775 --> 01:47:49.758
Make that baby an orphan
before he's born?

01:47:49.858 --> 01:47:51.860
Huh? Hmm?

01:47:52.541 --> 01:47:54.082
All right?

01:47:54.182 --> 01:47:57.406
You spic slobs
still betting Yankees?

01:47:57.506 --> 01:47:59.408
Tell them to stop
taking in action, all right?

01:47:59.508 --> 01:48:00.969
(COMMENTATOR NARRATING
BASEBALL GAME ON RADIO)

01:48:01.069 --> 01:48:03.071
We lost enough money
last weekend game.

01:48:09.318 --> 01:48:11.520
Oh. Come here,
come here, come here!

01:48:20.889 --> 01:48:23.252
(GRUNTING)

01:48:39.949 --> 01:48:41.951
(SCREAMING)

01:48:54.564 --> 01:48:56.566
(GROANING)

01:49:08.938 --> 01:49:11.861
If you touch
my sister again,
I'll kill you.

01:49:27.117 --> 01:49:28.258
(BELL TOLLING)

01:49:28.358 --> 01:49:30.360
(RECITING IN LATIN)

01:49:33.043 --> 01:49:35.365
(BAND PLAYING
TRADITIONAL MUSIC)

01:49:40.490 --> 01:49:42.492
(ALL APPLAUDING)

01:53:05.619 --> 01:53:09.803
Hey! We weren't
expecting you, Kay.
You should call.

01:53:09.903 --> 01:53:14.248
Yes, well, I have.
I mean, I've tried
writing and calling.

01:53:14.348 --> 01:53:16.410
Now I want
to reach Michael.

01:53:16.510 --> 01:53:18.172
Nobody knows
where he is.

01:53:18.272 --> 01:53:20.274
We know that
he's all right,
but that's all.

01:53:22.116 --> 01:53:24.658
Uh, what was that?

01:53:24.758 --> 01:53:28.022
Well that's an accident,
but nobody was hurt.

01:53:28.122 --> 01:53:33.668
Tom, will you give
this letter to Michael.
Please? Please.

01:53:33.768 --> 01:53:35.830
Well, if I accepted that,

01:53:35.930 --> 01:53:39.393
in a court of law,
they could prove that I have
knowledge of his whereabouts.

01:53:39.493 --> 01:53:41.836
Now you just be patient,
Kay. He'll get in touch
with you, all right?

01:53:41.936 --> 01:53:45.600
I let my cab go,
so can I come in to call
another one, please?

01:53:45.700 --> 01:53:47.642
Come on.
I'm sorry.
Come on.

01:53:47.742 --> 01:53:49.744
(KAY CLEARS THROAT)

01:53:54.308 --> 01:53:56.311
(TELEPHONE RINGING)

01:54:04.719 --> 01:54:08.343
Hello?

01:54:08.443 --> 01:54:10.025
WOMAN: (ON TELEPHONE)
Is Carlo there?

01:54:10.125 --> 01:54:11.346
Who is this?

01:54:11.446 --> 01:54:12.988
This is a friend of Carlo's.

01:54:13.088 --> 01:54:15.690
Would you tell him that
I can't make it tonight
until later?

01:54:22.017 --> 01:54:24.019
Bitch!

01:54:25.300 --> 01:54:26.361
Dinner's on the table.

01:54:26.461 --> 01:54:28.003
I'm not hungry yet.

01:54:28.103 --> 01:54:29.484
The food is on the table.
It's getting cold.

01:54:29.584 --> 01:54:31.486
I'll eat out later.

01:54:31.586 --> 01:54:33.168
You just told me
to make you dinner!

01:54:33.268 --> 01:54:35.090
(SPEAKS ITALIAN)
Vafangool!

01:54:35.190 --> 01:54:37.272
I'll vafangool you!

01:54:40.435 --> 01:54:41.977
(DISHES CLATTERING)

01:54:42.077 --> 01:54:44.920
She has a filthy mouth,
this little Guinea brat.

01:54:49.244 --> 01:54:53.389
That's it, break it all,
you spoiled Guinea brat.
Break it all!

01:54:53.489 --> 01:54:56.292
(SHOUTING INDISTINCTLY)

01:55:02.658 --> 01:55:05.461
Why don't you bring
your whore home for dinner?

01:55:07.062 --> 01:55:09.545
Maybe I will.
(SOBBING)

01:55:15.271 --> 01:55:16.933
Now clean it up!

01:55:17.033 --> 01:55:18.374
Like hell I will!

01:55:18.474 --> 01:55:22.458
You skinny, spoiled brat.
Clean it up! Clean it up!

01:55:22.558 --> 01:55:26.983
Clean it up!
I said, clean it up!
Clean it up!

01:55:27.083 --> 01:55:31.928
Clean it up. Clean it up!
Clean that up, you...

01:55:32.488 --> 01:55:35.111
(SCREAMING)

01:55:35.211 --> 01:55:36.873
Clean it!

01:55:36.973 --> 01:55:39.876
Clean it up! Yeah, yeah.
Come on now, kill me.

01:55:39.976 --> 01:55:41.438
Be a murderer,
like your father!

01:55:41.538 --> 01:55:43.159
Come on! All you Corleones
are murderers anyway!

01:55:43.259 --> 01:55:44.801
Come on!
I hate you!

01:55:44.901 --> 01:55:46.903
Come on, kill me!

01:55:48.144 --> 01:55:49.686
Get out of here!

01:55:49.786 --> 01:55:51.167
I hate you!

01:55:51.267 --> 01:55:53.290
Now I'll kill you.

01:55:53.390 --> 01:55:56.393
You Guinea brat.
Get out of here!

01:55:59.516 --> 01:56:01.518
(CONNIE SCREAMING)

01:56:05.442 --> 01:56:07.864
(BABY CRYING)
Connie, what's the matter?

01:56:07.964 --> 01:56:10.587
I can't hear you.
What is it?

01:56:10.687 --> 01:56:13.670
Connie, talk louder.
The baby's crying.

01:56:13.770 --> 01:56:16.273
Santino, I can't understand.
I don't know.
I don't understand.

01:56:16.373 --> 01:56:17.955
(SHUSHING)

01:56:18.055 --> 01:56:19.797
Yeah, Connie.

01:56:19.897 --> 01:56:21.899
(CRYING CONTINUES)

01:56:24.541 --> 01:56:26.543
Listen to me.
You wait there.

01:56:29.066 --> 01:56:31.588
No, you just wait there.

01:56:33.791 --> 01:56:36.013
Son of a bitch.

01:56:36.113 --> 01:56:37.615
Son of a bitch!

01:56:37.715 --> 01:56:39.957
What's the matter?
Sonny!
(GRUNTS)

01:56:43.320 --> 01:56:46.363
Open the goddamn gate!
Get off your ass.

01:56:54.372 --> 01:56:56.374
Sonny!

01:57:02.180 --> 01:57:04.182
Sonny.
Get out of here!

01:57:05.263 --> 01:57:07.265
Go after him, go on!

01:57:20.358 --> 01:57:22.360
(HORN HONKING)

01:57:26.284 --> 01:57:28.286
(TOLL BELL DINGS)

01:57:29.007 --> 01:57:31.009
(MAN CHATTERING ON RADIO)

01:57:36.855 --> 01:57:38.877
Son of a bitch.
Come on!

01:57:38.977 --> 01:57:40.398
(HORN BLARING)

01:57:40.498 --> 01:57:42.501
(COIN CLINKING)

01:58:01.160 --> 01:58:03.162
(SCREAMING)

01:58:17.416 --> 01:58:19.418
(TIRES SCREECHING)

01:58:26.065 --> 01:58:28.067
(CARS DRIVING OFF)

01:58:32.672 --> 01:58:34.674
(GLASS CLINKING)

01:59:27.728 --> 01:59:29.730
Give me a drop.

01:59:31.011 --> 01:59:33.013
(CLOCK TICKING)

01:59:34.695 --> 01:59:36.697
(GULPS)

01:59:37.858 --> 01:59:40.140
My wife is crying upstairs.

01:59:42.543 --> 01:59:45.025
I hear cars
coming to the house.

01:59:49.710 --> 01:59:52.573
Consigliere of mine,

01:59:52.673 --> 01:59:56.137
I think you should
tell your Don
what everyone seems to know.

01:59:56.237 --> 01:59:59.460
I didn't
tell Mama anything.

01:59:59.560 --> 02:00:02.883
I was about
to come up and wake you
just now and tell you.

02:00:06.407 --> 02:00:08.409
But you needed
a drink first.

02:00:10.931 --> 02:00:12.934
Yeah.

02:00:15.216 --> 02:00:17.258
Well, now
you've had your drink.

02:00:23.504 --> 02:00:27.588
They shot Sonny
on the causeway.
He's dead.

02:00:31.112 --> 02:00:32.734
(SIGHS)

02:00:32.834 --> 02:00:34.836
(CLOCK TICKING)

02:00:45.206 --> 02:00:47.208
I want no inquiries made.

02:00:51.453 --> 02:00:53.975
I want no acts of vengeance.

02:00:55.737 --> 02:00:57.739
I want you
to arrange a meeting

02:00:59.421 --> 02:01:01.623
with the heads
of the five families.

02:01:04.025 --> 02:01:06.228
This war stops now.

02:01:27.409 --> 02:01:29.892
(CLEARS THROAT)
Call Bonasera.

02:01:30.813 --> 02:01:32.815
I need him now.

02:01:38.020 --> 02:01:40.022
(CONTINUES DIALING)

02:01:45.388 --> 02:01:50.253
This is Tom Hagen.
I'm calling for Vito Corleone,
at his request.

02:01:50.353 --> 02:01:52.975
Now, you owe
your Don a service.

02:01:53.075 --> 02:01:56.619
He has no doubt
that you will repay it.

02:01:56.719 --> 02:02:00.923
He will be at your
funeral parlor in one hour.
Be there to greet him.

02:02:22.345 --> 02:02:27.090
Well, my friend,
are you ready
to do me this service?

02:02:27.190 --> 02:02:30.473
Yes. What do you want
me to do?

02:02:38.562 --> 02:02:43.246
I want you to
use all your powers
and all your skills.

02:02:47.210 --> 02:02:49.373
I don't want his mother
to see him this way.

02:02:51.054 --> 02:02:53.056
(INHALES SHARPLY)

02:03:06.190 --> 02:03:08.872
Look how
they massacred my boy.

02:03:17.962 --> 02:03:19.944
(LAUGHING)

02:03:20.044 --> 02:03:22.046
(BOTH SPEAKING ITALIAN)

02:03:30.374 --> 02:03:32.376
(APOLLONIA LAUGHING)

02:03:37.141 --> 02:03:39.143
(SPEAKING ITALIAN)

02:03:43.988 --> 02:03:49.133
Monday, Tuesday, Thursday,
Wednesday, Friday,
Sunday, Saturday.

02:03:49.233 --> 02:03:51.236
(HORN HONKING)

02:04:56.942 --> 02:04:58.444
(CAR HONKING)

02:04:58.544 --> 02:05:00.546
(SPEAKING ITALIAN)

02:05:20.166 --> 02:05:22.168
Fabrizio! (SPEAKS ITALIAN)

02:05:23.289 --> 02:05:24.310
(IN ENGLISH)

02:05:24.410 --> 02:05:27.033
Are you driving
yourself, boss?
Yes.

02:05:27.133 --> 02:05:29.035
Is your wife
coming with you?

02:05:29.135 --> 02:05:31.958
No, I want you to take her
to her father's house
until I know things are safe.

02:05:32.058 --> 02:05:34.060
Okay, anything
you say, boss.

02:05:38.945 --> 02:05:40.947
(BOTH SPEAKING ITALIAN)

02:06:04.371 --> 02:06:06.373
Fabrizio!

02:06:08.815 --> 02:06:10.817
(CAR HONKING)
(APOLLONIA SPEAKS ITALAIN)

02:06:18.866 --> 02:06:20.868
No! No, Apollonia!

02:06:43.491 --> 02:06:45.433
VITO: Don Barzini,
I want to thank you

02:06:45.533 --> 02:06:49.317
for helping me organize
this meeting in a day,

02:06:49.417 --> 02:06:54.302
and also the other heads
of the five families
from New York and New Jersey.

02:06:56.063 --> 02:06:59.167
Carmine Cuneo
from the Bronx,

02:06:59.267 --> 02:07:02.670
and from Brooklyn

02:07:04.312 --> 02:07:06.394
Philip Tattaglia.

02:07:08.036 --> 02:07:10.899
And from Staten Island

02:07:10.999 --> 02:07:14.382
we have with us
Victor Strachi.

02:07:14.482 --> 02:07:20.108
And the other associates
that came as far as from
California and Kansas City

02:07:20.208 --> 02:07:24.012
and all the other territories
of the country. Thank you.

02:07:30.699 --> 02:07:32.901
How did things
ever get so far?

02:07:34.262 --> 02:07:36.264
I don't know.

02:07:37.946 --> 02:07:41.430
It was so unfortunate,
so unnecessary.

02:07:44.553 --> 02:07:48.156
Tattaglia lost a son,
and I lost a son.

02:07:50.439 --> 02:07:53.822
We're quits.
And if Tattaglia agrees,

02:07:53.922 --> 02:07:59.268
then I'm willing
to let things go on
the way they were before.

02:07:59.368 --> 02:08:03.072
We're all grateful
to Don Corleone
for calling this meeting.

02:08:03.172 --> 02:08:05.754
We all know him
as a man of his word.

02:08:05.854 --> 02:08:08.357
A modest man who
always listens to reason.

02:08:08.457 --> 02:08:12.722
Yes, Don Barzini.
He's too modest.

02:08:12.822 --> 02:08:15.825
He had all the judges
and politicians
in his pocket.

02:08:17.106 --> 02:08:19.929
He refused to share them.

02:08:20.029 --> 02:08:23.853
When did I ever refuse
an accommodation?

02:08:23.953 --> 02:08:25.955
All of you know me here.

02:08:27.196 --> 02:08:32.401
When did I ever refuse,
except one time? And why?

02:08:34.083 --> 02:08:35.505
Because I believe

02:08:35.605 --> 02:08:39.789
this drug business
is gonna destroy us
in the years to come.

02:08:39.889 --> 02:08:44.234
I mean, it's not like gambling
or liquor or even women,

02:08:44.334 --> 02:08:46.596
which is something
that most people want
nowadays,

02:08:46.696 --> 02:08:50.320
but is forbidden to them
by the pezzonovante
of the Church.

02:08:50.420 --> 02:08:52.001
Even the police departments

02:08:52.101 --> 02:08:55.125
that have helped us
in the past with
gambling and other things

02:08:55.225 --> 02:08:56.406
are going to refuse to help us

02:08:56.506 --> 02:08:59.449
when it comes to narcotics.

02:08:59.549 --> 02:09:04.734
And I believed that then
and I believe that now.

02:09:04.834 --> 02:09:06.897
Times have changed.

02:09:06.997 --> 02:09:11.822
It's not like the old days,
and we can do
anything we want.

02:09:11.922 --> 02:09:14.665
A refusal is not
the act of a friend.

02:09:14.765 --> 02:09:18.749
If Don Corleone
had all the judges
and politicians in New York,

02:09:18.849 --> 02:09:20.510
then he must share them

02:09:20.610 --> 02:09:25.836
or let others use them.
He must let us draw
the water from the well.

02:09:25.936 --> 02:09:29.520
Certainly
he can present a bill
for such services.

02:09:29.620 --> 02:09:32.523
After all,
we're not communists.

02:09:32.623 --> 02:09:35.245
(ALL LAUGH)

02:09:35.345 --> 02:09:38.489
I also don't believe
in drugs.

02:09:38.589 --> 02:09:40.731
For years, I paid
my people extra,

02:09:40.831 --> 02:09:43.374
so they wouldn't
do that kind of business.

02:09:43.474 --> 02:09:46.577
Somebody comes to them
and says, "I have powders.

02:09:46.677 --> 02:09:50.261
"If you put up
3-4,000 dollar investment,

02:09:50.361 --> 02:09:52.923
"we can make
50,000 distributing."

02:09:54.245 --> 02:09:55.746
So they can't resist.

02:09:55.846 --> 02:10:00.191
I want to control it
as a business,
to keep it respectable.

02:10:00.291 --> 02:10:02.353
I don't want it
near schools,

02:10:02.453 --> 02:10:04.455
I don't want it
sold to children.

02:10:05.136 --> 02:10:08.079
That's an infamia.

02:10:08.179 --> 02:10:12.163
In my city we would keep
the traffic and the
dark people, the colored.

02:10:12.263 --> 02:10:15.226
They're animals anyway,
so let them
lose their souls.

02:10:22.073 --> 02:10:25.677
I hoped that
we could come here
and reason together.

02:10:27.118 --> 02:10:28.460
And as a reasonable man,

02:10:28.560 --> 02:10:30.502
I'm willing to do
whatever is necessary

02:10:30.602 --> 02:10:34.225
to find a peaceful solution
to this problem.

02:10:34.325 --> 02:10:36.187
Then we are agreed.

02:10:36.287 --> 02:10:38.630
The traffic in drugs
will be permitted,
but controlled.

02:10:38.730 --> 02:10:43.195
And Don Corleone will give us
protection in the east,
and there will be the peace.

02:10:43.295 --> 02:10:47.038
But I must have
strict assurance
from Corleone.

02:10:47.138 --> 02:10:50.442
As time goes by
and his position
becomes stronger,

02:10:50.542 --> 02:10:53.165
will he attempt
any individual vendetta?

02:10:53.265 --> 02:10:54.926
BARZINI: Look, we are all
reasonable men here.

02:10:55.026 --> 02:10:58.410
We don't have to give
assurances as if
we were lawyers.

02:10:58.510 --> 02:11:01.333
You talk about
vengeance.

02:11:01.433 --> 02:11:04.196
Is vengeance gonna
bring your son back to you?

02:11:04.836 --> 02:11:06.839
Or my boy to me?

02:11:07.519 --> 02:11:09.842
I forgo the vengeance
of my son.

02:11:13.085 --> 02:11:15.087
But I have
selfish reasons.

02:11:17.690 --> 02:11:21.253
My youngest son was forced
to leave this country

02:11:23.095 --> 02:11:25.377
because of this
Sollozzo business.

02:11:25.978 --> 02:11:27.400
All right.

02:11:27.500 --> 02:11:31.163
And I have to make
arrangements to bring
him back here safely.

02:11:31.263 --> 02:11:33.506
Cleared of all these
false charges.

02:11:35.307 --> 02:11:37.309
But I'm
a superstitious man.

02:11:38.591 --> 02:11:41.013
And if some unlucky accident
should befall him,

02:11:41.113 --> 02:11:43.876
if he should get shot
in the head
by a police officer,

02:11:45.238 --> 02:11:48.821
or if he should hang himself
in his jail cell,

02:11:48.921 --> 02:11:51.484
or if he's struck
by a bolt of lightning,

02:11:53.045 --> 02:11:56.129
then I'm going to blame
some of the people
in this room.

02:11:58.251 --> 02:12:00.253
And that I do not forgive.

02:12:03.216 --> 02:12:05.578
But, that aside

02:12:08.661 --> 02:12:10.663
let me say that I swear

02:12:12.625 --> 02:12:15.689
on the souls
of my grandchildren,

02:12:15.789 --> 02:12:19.312
that I will not be the one
to break the peace
we've made here today.

02:12:45.739 --> 02:12:47.361
When I meet
with the Tattaglia people,

02:12:47.461 --> 02:12:51.165
should I insist that all
his drug middlemen
have clean records?

02:12:51.265 --> 02:12:53.267
Mention it.
Don't insist.

02:12:55.349 --> 02:12:57.992
Barzini is a man
who will know that
without being told.

02:12:59.193 --> 02:13:01.195
You mean Tattaglia.

02:13:01.916 --> 02:13:03.918
Tattaglia's a pimp.

02:13:04.999 --> 02:13:07.201
He could never
have outfought Santino.

02:13:10.524 --> 02:13:12.306
But I didn't know
until this day

02:13:12.406 --> 02:13:16.130
that it was Barzini
all along.

02:13:31.466 --> 02:13:33.468
Come on, Nancy.

02:13:34.869 --> 02:13:37.392
Keep together,
everyone. Brian.

02:13:38.873 --> 02:13:40.875
Okay, all right.

02:13:53.568 --> 02:13:55.570
How long
have you been back?

02:13:56.571 --> 02:13:58.573
I've been back a year.

02:13:59.894 --> 02:14:01.897
Longer than that, I think.

02:14:04.739 --> 02:14:06.741
It's good to see you, Kay.

02:14:12.948 --> 02:14:15.310
Hi, Ms. Adams.
(CYCLE BELL TRILLS)

02:14:15.911 --> 02:14:17.813
(DOG BARKING)

02:14:17.913 --> 02:14:19.915
I'm working for
my father now, Kay.

02:14:22.958 --> 02:14:25.961
He's been sick.
Very sick.

02:14:27.483 --> 02:14:29.385
But you're not
like him, Michael.

02:14:29.485 --> 02:14:32.227
I thought you weren't
going to become a man
like your father.

02:14:32.327 --> 02:14:34.330
That's what you told me.

02:14:35.250 --> 02:14:38.033
My father is no different
than any other powerful man.

02:14:38.133 --> 02:14:39.555
(SCOFFS)

02:14:39.655 --> 02:14:43.098
Any man who's responsible
for other people.

02:14:44.340 --> 02:14:46.722
Like a senator
or president.

02:14:46.822 --> 02:14:48.084
You know
how naive you sound.

02:14:48.184 --> 02:14:49.325
Why?

02:14:49.425 --> 02:14:51.867
Senators and presidents
don't have men killed.

02:14:53.429 --> 02:14:55.091
Oh.

02:14:55.191 --> 02:14:57.193
Who's being naive, Kay?

02:14:58.514 --> 02:15:01.778
Kay, my father's way
of doing things is over.
It's finished.

02:15:01.878 --> 02:15:03.880
Even he knows that.

02:15:04.320 --> 02:15:05.742
I mean, in five years

02:15:05.842 --> 02:15:08.364
the Corleone family
is going to be
completely legitimate.

02:15:10.606 --> 02:15:14.610
Trust me.
That's all I can tell you
about my business. Kay...

02:15:15.932 --> 02:15:19.115
Michael, why did
you come here? Why?

02:15:19.215 --> 02:15:20.997
(SOBS)

02:15:21.097 --> 02:15:25.241
What do you want with me
after all this time?
I've been calling and writing.

02:15:25.341 --> 02:15:27.324
I came because I need you.

02:15:27.424 --> 02:15:28.765
Because I care for you.

02:15:28.865 --> 02:15:30.046
Please stop it, Michael.

02:15:30.146 --> 02:15:32.789
Because...
I want you to marry me.

02:15:34.431 --> 02:15:35.572
It's too late.
It's too late.

02:15:35.672 --> 02:15:38.615
Please, Kay...

02:15:38.715 --> 02:15:42.719
I'll do anything you ask.
Anything to make up
for what's happened to us.

02:15:44.521 --> 02:15:46.823
Because
that's important, Kay.

02:15:46.923 --> 02:15:50.107
Because what's
important is that

02:15:50.207 --> 02:15:53.650
we have each other.
That we have
a life together.

02:15:55.052 --> 02:15:56.713
That we have children.

02:15:56.813 --> 02:15:58.815
Our children.

02:15:59.336 --> 02:16:01.578
Kay, I need you.

02:16:03.460 --> 02:16:05.462
And I love you.

02:16:27.405 --> 02:16:30.948
TESSIO: Barzini's people
chisel my territory
and we do nothing about it!

02:16:31.048 --> 02:16:33.471
Pretty soon I there won't be
one place in Brooklyn
I can hang my hat!

02:16:33.571 --> 02:16:35.273
MICHAEL: Just be patient.

02:16:35.373 --> 02:16:37.875
TESSIO: I'm not asking you
for help, Mike
Just take off the handcuffs.

02:16:37.975 --> 02:16:39.157
MICHAEL: Be patient.

02:16:39.257 --> 02:16:41.119
CARLO: We got to
protect ourselves.

02:16:41.219 --> 02:16:43.201
Give me a chance
to recruit some new men.

02:16:43.301 --> 02:16:44.722
MICHAEL: No.

02:16:44.822 --> 02:16:47.485
I don't want to give
Barzini an excuse
to start fighting.

02:16:47.585 --> 02:16:49.587
TESSIO: Mike, you're wrong.

02:16:50.108 --> 02:16:52.370
CLEMENZA: Don Corleone...

02:16:52.470 --> 02:16:54.052
You once said that
the day would come

02:16:54.152 --> 02:16:56.534
when Tessio and me
could form our own family.

02:16:56.634 --> 02:16:58.536
Till today
I would never think of it.

02:16:58.636 --> 02:17:00.638
I must ask
your permission.

02:17:01.719 --> 02:17:04.382
Michael is now
head of the family

02:17:04.482 --> 02:17:07.445
and if he
gives his permission,
then you have my blessing.

02:17:08.887 --> 02:17:11.229
After we make
the move to Nevada,

02:17:11.329 --> 02:17:14.352
you can break off
from the Corleone family
and go on your own.

02:17:14.452 --> 02:17:15.714
After we make
the move to Nevada.

02:17:15.814 --> 02:17:17.816
TESSIO:
How long will that be?

02:17:18.817 --> 02:17:20.038
Six months.

02:17:20.138 --> 02:17:23.442
Forgive me, Godfather,
but with you gone,

02:17:23.542 --> 02:17:26.485
me and Pete will come
under Barzini's thumb
sooner or later.

02:17:26.585 --> 02:17:28.647
And I hate that
goddamn Barzini.

02:17:28.747 --> 02:17:32.130
In six months' time
there will be
nothing left to build on.

02:17:32.230 --> 02:17:34.052
Do you have faith
in my judgment?

02:17:34.152 --> 02:17:35.174
Yes.

02:17:35.274 --> 02:17:36.695
Do I have your loyalty?

02:17:36.795 --> 02:17:38.137
Yes, always, Godfather.

02:17:38.237 --> 02:17:40.299
Then be a friend to Michael.

02:17:40.399 --> 02:17:42.401
Do as he says.

02:17:46.405 --> 02:17:48.107
There are things
being negotiated now

02:17:48.207 --> 02:17:51.750
that are gonna solve
all your problems
and answer all your questions.

02:17:51.850 --> 02:17:53.852
That's all
I can tell you now.

02:17:55.014 --> 02:17:57.556
Carlo, you grew up
in Nevada.

02:17:57.656 --> 02:18:00.019
When we make our move there,
you'll be my right-hand man.

02:18:01.180 --> 02:18:03.182
Tom Hagen
is no longer consigliere.

02:18:03.662 --> 02:18:05.925
He'll be our lawyer in Vegas.

02:18:06.025 --> 02:18:08.608
That's no reflection on Tom,
just how I want it.

02:18:08.708 --> 02:18:10.489
Besides, if I ever need help,

02:18:10.589 --> 02:18:12.572
who's a better consigliere
than my father?

02:18:12.672 --> 02:18:14.674
Well, that's it.

02:18:33.413 --> 02:18:34.434
Thank you, Papa.

02:18:34.534 --> 02:18:36.536
I'm happy
for you, Carlo.

02:18:37.417 --> 02:18:40.220
Mike... Why am I out?

02:18:41.741 --> 02:18:43.863
You're not
a wartime consigliere, Tom.

02:18:45.705 --> 02:18:48.348
Things may get rough
with the move we're trying.

02:18:49.029 --> 02:18:51.031
Tom.

02:18:55.515 --> 02:18:57.818
I advised Michael.

02:18:57.918 --> 02:19:00.741
I never thought
you were a bad consigliere.

02:19:00.841 --> 02:19:05.005
I thought Santino
was a bad Don,
rest in peace.

02:19:06.366 --> 02:19:10.470
Michael has
all my confidence,
just as you do.

02:19:10.570 --> 02:19:15.616
But there are reasons
why you must have no part
in what is going to happen.

02:19:16.697 --> 02:19:18.278
Maybe I could help.

02:19:18.378 --> 02:19:20.380
You're out, Tom.

02:19:29.870 --> 02:19:31.872
(DOOR CLOSING)

02:20:08.830 --> 02:20:11.653
I can't get over the way
your face looks.

02:20:11.753 --> 02:20:13.134
It really looks good!

02:20:13.234 --> 02:20:15.697
This doctor did some job.
Who talked you into it?

02:20:15.797 --> 02:20:17.779
Kay? Hey, hey, hey!
Wait. Hey, hey.

02:20:17.879 --> 02:20:19.741
Leave them out here.
We'll deal with them later.

02:20:19.841 --> 02:20:22.143
He's tired and wants
to clean up. All right now.

02:20:22.243 --> 02:20:24.245
Let me open the door,
all right?

02:20:25.927 --> 02:20:28.450
(PLAYING
FOR HE'S A JOLLY GOOD FELLOW)

02:20:30.892 --> 02:20:32.994
Hello, Mike!
Welcome to Las Vegas!

02:20:33.094 --> 02:20:36.318
All for you, kid! Huh?
It's all his idea, right?

02:20:36.418 --> 02:20:37.679
JOHNNY: Your brother Freddy.

02:20:37.779 --> 02:20:38.760
FREDO: Girls?
(BOTH LAUGH)

02:20:38.860 --> 02:20:40.862
Fredo...
Huh?

02:20:42.744 --> 02:20:45.807
I'll be right back.
You keep them occupied.

02:20:45.907 --> 02:20:46.929
Atta boy, huh?

02:20:47.029 --> 02:20:49.251
Anything you want, kid,
anything. Huh?

02:20:49.351 --> 02:20:51.353
Who are the girls?

02:20:51.954 --> 02:20:53.896
That's for you
to find out.

02:20:53.996 --> 02:20:55.998
Get rid of them, Fredo.

02:20:56.959 --> 02:20:58.620
Hey, Mike...

02:20:58.720 --> 02:21:01.583
Fredo, I'm here on business.
I leave tomorrow.
Now get rid of them.

02:21:01.683 --> 02:21:04.366
I'm tired.
Get rid of the band too.

02:21:10.292 --> 02:21:13.235
Hey, just take off.
Come on. Take off. Let's go.

02:21:13.335 --> 02:21:15.457
Come on. Hey, that's it.
Hey, Angelo.

02:21:16.659 --> 02:21:19.602
Come on, let's go.
Hey, come on! Scram!

02:21:19.702 --> 02:21:21.203
(MUSIC STOPS)

02:21:21.303 --> 02:21:23.406
Come on, honey. Let's go.
I don't know, Johnny.

02:21:23.506 --> 02:21:24.807
What the hell's
the matter with him?

02:21:24.907 --> 02:21:26.909
I'm sorry.
Sorry... Sorry.

02:21:28.190 --> 02:21:30.713
I don't know.
He's tired.

02:21:32.034 --> 02:21:34.036
(SIGHS)

02:21:36.359 --> 02:21:37.660
(DOOR CLOSING)

02:21:37.760 --> 02:21:39.762
What happened
to Moe Greene?

02:21:40.923 --> 02:21:42.265
He said he had
some business.

02:21:42.365 --> 02:21:45.228
He said to give him a call
when the party started.

02:21:45.328 --> 02:21:47.330
Well, give him a call.
(PATS ON BACK)

02:21:48.651 --> 02:21:49.993
Johnny, how are you?

02:21:50.093 --> 02:21:51.835
Hello, Mike.
Nice to see you again.

02:21:51.935 --> 02:21:52.956
MICHAEL:
We're proud of you.

02:21:53.056 --> 02:21:54.117
JOHNNY: Thanks, Mike.

02:21:54.217 --> 02:21:56.399
Sit down, Johnny,
I want to talk to you.

02:21:56.499 --> 02:21:57.761
The Don is proud
too, Johnny.

02:21:57.861 --> 02:22:00.924
Well, I owe it
all to him.

02:22:01.024 --> 02:22:02.886
Well, he knows
how grateful you are.

02:22:02.986 --> 02:22:06.129
That's why
he'd like to ask
a favor of you.

02:22:06.229 --> 02:22:08.231
Mike, what can I do?

02:22:09.392 --> 02:22:11.815
The Corleone family
is thinking of giving up
all its interests

02:22:11.915 --> 02:22:15.499
in the olive oil business
and settling out here.

02:22:15.599 --> 02:22:18.181
Now Moe Greene
will sell us his share
of the casino

02:22:18.281 --> 02:22:21.024
and the hotel, so
it could completely
be owned by the family.

02:22:21.124 --> 02:22:23.827
Tom!
Hey, Mike, are you
sure about that?

02:22:23.927 --> 02:22:26.870
Moe loves the business.
He never said nothing
to me about selling.

02:22:26.970 --> 02:22:29.132
Yeah, I'll make him an offer
he can't refuse.

02:22:30.974 --> 02:22:32.976
See, Johnny...

02:22:33.457 --> 02:22:34.998
See, we figure
that entertainment

02:22:35.098 --> 02:22:37.681
will be a big factor
in drawing gamblers
to the casino.

02:22:37.781 --> 02:22:39.403
And we hope
you'll sign a contract

02:22:39.503 --> 02:22:41.505
to appear
five times a year.

02:22:44.428 --> 02:22:49.153
Perhaps convince
some of your friends
in the movies to do the same.

02:22:50.354 --> 02:22:52.356
We're counting on you.

02:22:54.478 --> 02:22:57.101
Sure, Mike.
I'll do anything
for my godfather.

02:22:57.201 --> 02:22:59.203
You know that.
Good.

02:23:01.165 --> 02:23:05.830
Hey, Mike! Hello, fellows.
Everybody's here.
Freddy, Tom.

02:23:05.930 --> 02:23:07.191
Good to see you, Mike.

02:23:07.291 --> 02:23:08.472
How are you, Moe?
All right.

02:23:08.572 --> 02:23:09.554
Did you get
everything you want?

02:23:09.654 --> 02:23:11.115
The chef cooked
for you special,

02:23:11.215 --> 02:23:13.638
the dancers will kick
your tongue out
and your credit is good!

02:23:13.738 --> 02:23:16.340
Draw chips for everybody
in the room so
they can play on the house.

02:23:20.064 --> 02:23:21.686
My credit good enough
to buy you out?

02:23:21.786 --> 02:23:23.788
(LAUGHING)

02:23:24.509 --> 02:23:26.331
Buy me out?

02:23:26.431 --> 02:23:29.013
The casino, the hotel.

02:23:29.113 --> 02:23:32.016
The Corleone family
wants to buy you out.

02:23:32.116 --> 02:23:34.859
The Corleone family
wants to buy me out?

02:23:34.959 --> 02:23:37.502
No, I buy you out.
You don't buy me out.

02:23:37.602 --> 02:23:41.026
Your casino loses money.
Maybe we can do better.

02:23:41.126 --> 02:23:43.128
You think I'm skimming
off the top, Mike?

02:23:44.289 --> 02:23:46.291
You're unlucky.

02:23:47.012 --> 02:23:49.674
(CHUCKLING)

02:23:49.774 --> 02:23:52.277
You goddamn Guineas
really make me laugh.

02:23:52.377 --> 02:23:53.999
I do you a favor
and take Freddy in

02:23:54.099 --> 02:23:55.560
when you're having
a bad time,

02:23:55.660 --> 02:23:58.163
and now you try
to push me out!
MICHAEL: Wait a minute.

02:23:58.263 --> 02:24:01.767
You took Freddy in because
the Corleone family
bankrolled your Casino,

02:24:01.867 --> 02:24:05.130
because the Molinari family
on the coast
guaranteed his safety.

02:24:05.230 --> 02:24:07.132
Now we're talking business.
Let's talk business.

02:24:07.232 --> 02:24:08.574
Yeah, let's talk
business, Mike.

02:24:08.674 --> 02:24:10.175
First of all,
you're all done.

02:24:10.275 --> 02:24:12.578
The Corleone family
don't have that kind
of muscle anymore.

02:24:12.678 --> 02:24:14.460
The Godfather is sick, right?

02:24:14.560 --> 02:24:17.022
You're getting chased out
of New York by Barzini
and the other families.

02:24:17.122 --> 02:24:18.424
What do you think is going on?

02:24:18.524 --> 02:24:21.026
You think you can come
to my hotel
and take over?

02:24:21.126 --> 02:24:26.031
I talked to Barzini.
I can make a deal with him
and still keep my hotel!

02:24:26.131 --> 02:24:29.635
Is that why
you slapped my brother
around in public?

02:24:29.735 --> 02:24:34.480
Ah, no, that was nothing,
Mike. Now, Moe didn't mean
nothing by that.

02:24:34.580 --> 02:24:36.922
Sure he flies off the handle
once in a while,

02:24:37.022 --> 02:24:38.965
but Moe and me
we're good friends,
right Moe, huh?

02:24:39.065 --> 02:24:40.926
I've got a business to run.

02:24:41.026 --> 02:24:43.769
I've got to kick asses
sometimes to make it
run right.

02:24:43.869 --> 02:24:45.251
We had a little argument,
Freddy and I,

02:24:45.351 --> 02:24:47.353
so I had
to straighten him out.

02:24:47.873 --> 02:24:49.875
You straightened
my brother out?

02:24:50.596 --> 02:24:53.219
He was banging
cocktail waitresses
two at a time!

02:24:53.319 --> 02:24:56.122
Players couldn't get a drink
at the table.
What's wrong with you?

02:25:02.088 --> 02:25:05.632
I leave for New York tomorrow.
Think about a price.

02:25:05.732 --> 02:25:07.674
(DRINK SPILLING)
MOE: Son of a bitch!

02:25:07.774 --> 02:25:10.557
Do you know who I am?
I'm Moe Greene!

02:25:10.657 --> 02:25:13.039
I made my bones when you were
going out with cheerleaders.

02:25:13.139 --> 02:25:15.421
Wait a minute, Moe.
Moe, I got an idea.

02:25:16.663 --> 02:25:18.805
Tom, Tom,
you're the consigliere.

02:25:18.905 --> 02:25:20.246
You can talk to the Don...
You can explain...

02:25:20.346 --> 02:25:22.088
Just a minute now.

02:25:22.188 --> 02:25:25.612
Don is semi-retired
and Mike is in charge
of the family business now.

02:25:25.712 --> 02:25:28.555
If you have
anything to say,
say it to Michael.

02:25:32.479 --> 02:25:34.341
(DOOR SLAMMING)

02:25:34.441 --> 02:25:37.924
Mike, you don't come
to Las Vegas and talk to a man
like Moe Greene like that!

02:25:39.686 --> 02:25:41.688
Fredo...

02:25:42.089 --> 02:25:44.571
You're my older brother,
and I love you.

02:25:46.293 --> 02:25:49.776
But don't ever take sides
with anyone
against the family again.

02:25:51.859 --> 02:25:53.861
Ever.

02:26:00.988 --> 02:26:04.011
I have to see my father
and his people,
so have dinner without me.

02:26:04.111 --> 02:26:06.113
Oh, Michael.

02:26:06.914 --> 02:26:08.576
This weekend we'll go out.
Mmm.

02:26:08.676 --> 02:26:11.599
We'll go to the city,
we'll see a show and we'll
have dinner. I promise.

02:26:12.119 --> 02:26:14.121
Mmm.

02:26:19.166 --> 02:26:22.189
Oh, Michael., Michael,
your sister wants
to ask you something.

02:26:22.289 --> 02:26:23.311
Let her ask.

02:26:23.411 --> 02:26:24.952
No, she's afraid to.

02:26:25.052 --> 02:26:27.475
Connie and Carlo
want you to be godfather
to their little boy.

02:26:27.575 --> 02:26:29.317
We'll see.
Will you?

02:26:29.417 --> 02:26:31.419
Let me think about it.
We'll see. Come on.
Michael, come on.

02:26:38.546 --> 02:26:40.488
So...

02:26:40.588 --> 02:26:43.491
Barzini will move
against you first.

02:26:43.591 --> 02:26:46.995
He'll set up a meeting
with someone
that you absolutely trust.

02:26:48.156 --> 02:26:50.158
Guaranteeing your safety.

02:26:51.319 --> 02:26:53.962
And at that meeting
you'll be assassinated.

02:26:59.287 --> 02:27:01.810
I like to drink wine
more than I used to.

02:27:03.611 --> 02:27:05.834
Anyway,
I'm drinking more.

02:27:05.934 --> 02:27:07.936
It's good for you, Pop.

02:27:12.340 --> 02:27:14.342
I don't know.

02:27:15.744 --> 02:27:17.746
Your wife and children,
are you happy with them?

02:27:19.508 --> 02:27:21.410
Very happy.

02:27:21.510 --> 02:27:24.173
That's good.

02:27:24.273 --> 02:27:29.218
I hope you don't mind
the way I keep going over
this Barzini business.

02:27:29.318 --> 02:27:31.180
No, not at all.

02:27:31.280 --> 02:27:33.622
It's an old habit.

02:27:33.722 --> 02:27:36.245
I spend my life trying
not to be careless.

02:27:38.167 --> 02:27:41.250
Women and children
can be careless,
but not men.

02:27:44.533 --> 02:27:46.235
How's your boy?

02:27:46.335 --> 02:27:47.396
He's good.

02:27:47.496 --> 02:27:49.698
You know, he looks
more like you every day.

02:27:52.982 --> 02:27:55.364
He's smarter than I am.

02:27:55.464 --> 02:27:57.466
Three years old and he can
read the funny papers.

02:27:59.508 --> 02:28:01.510
Read the funny papers.

02:28:06.756 --> 02:28:08.578
Uh...

02:28:08.678 --> 02:28:11.220
I want you to arrange
to have a telephone man

02:28:11.320 --> 02:28:14.424
check all the calls that go
in and out of here...

02:28:14.524 --> 02:28:17.787
I did it already, Pop.
I took care of that.
It could be anyone.

02:28:17.887 --> 02:28:19.889
Oh, that's right. I forgot.

02:28:23.893 --> 02:28:25.895
What's the matter?

02:28:26.536 --> 02:28:28.538
What's bothering you?

02:28:32.061 --> 02:28:34.364
I'll handle it.

02:28:34.464 --> 02:28:36.546
I told you I can handle it,
I'll handle it.

02:28:49.960 --> 02:28:53.163
I knew that Santino
was gonna have to
go through all this.

02:28:54.524 --> 02:28:56.226
And Fredo...

02:28:56.326 --> 02:28:58.328
Well...

02:28:58.889 --> 02:29:00.891
Fredo was, well...

02:29:02.813 --> 02:29:05.656
But I never...
I never wanted
this for you.

02:29:07.978 --> 02:29:09.239
I worked my whole life.

02:29:09.339 --> 02:29:12.963
I don't apologize
to take care of my family.

02:29:13.063 --> 02:29:16.967
And I refused
to be a fool,

02:29:17.067 --> 02:29:21.191
dancing on a string
held by
all those big shots.

02:29:23.193 --> 02:29:26.317
I don't apologize.
That's my life,
but I thought that...

02:29:28.319 --> 02:29:30.901
That when it was
your time, that...

02:29:31.001 --> 02:29:33.524
That you would be
the one to hold the strings.

02:29:35.246 --> 02:29:40.992
Senator Corleone.
Governor Corleone.
Something.

02:29:41.092 --> 02:29:43.094
Another pezzonovante.

02:29:44.135 --> 02:29:46.137
Well...

02:29:47.458 --> 02:29:48.880
(SIGHS)

02:29:48.980 --> 02:29:52.924
Just wasn't
enough time, Michael.
Wasn't enough time.

02:29:53.024 --> 02:29:56.547
We'll get there, Pop.
We'll get there.

02:29:57.628 --> 02:29:59.631
Hmm.

02:30:01.352 --> 02:30:05.817
Now listen,
whoever comes to you
with this Barzini meeting,

02:30:05.917 --> 02:30:08.840
he's the traitor.
Don't forget that.

02:30:26.017 --> 02:30:28.120
Can I hold it, please?

02:30:28.220 --> 02:30:30.222
(TALKING INDISTINCTLY)

02:30:43.275 --> 02:30:44.897
Can I water these?

02:30:44.997 --> 02:30:47.099
Yes, go ahead.

02:30:47.199 --> 02:30:49.962
Over here, over here.

02:30:51.844 --> 02:30:54.326
Be careful.
You're spilling it.

02:30:55.487 --> 02:30:57.489
(CLEARS THROAT)

02:30:58.290 --> 02:31:00.292
(ANTHONY LAUGHING)

02:31:00.853 --> 02:31:02.114
Anthony.

02:31:02.214 --> 02:31:04.216
Come here, come here.

02:31:05.858 --> 02:31:07.860
Come here.

02:31:09.221 --> 02:31:11.904
That's it.
We'll put it right there.

02:31:13.466 --> 02:31:15.468
(SIGHING)

02:31:17.430 --> 02:31:20.112
I'll show you something.
Come here. Come here.

02:31:21.794 --> 02:31:23.796
Stand there.

02:31:27.400 --> 02:31:29.402
Give me an orange!

02:31:32.445 --> 02:31:34.447
(GROWLING)

02:31:35.808 --> 02:31:37.430
(ANTHONY CRYING)

02:31:37.530 --> 02:31:39.532
(VITO LAUGHING)

02:31:47.540 --> 02:31:49.542
That's a new trick.

02:31:50.303 --> 02:31:52.665
You run in there.
Run in there.

02:32:05.118 --> 02:32:06.179
(VITO LAUGHING)

02:32:06.279 --> 02:32:08.281
ANTHONY: Where are you?

02:32:13.607 --> 02:32:15.609
(COUGHING)

02:32:16.129 --> 02:32:18.131
(ANTHONY LAUGHING)

02:32:22.736 --> 02:32:24.638
(COUGHING CONTINUES)
(ANTHONY SPEAKING
INDISTINCTLY)

02:32:24.738 --> 02:32:27.621
(GROANING)

02:32:29.183 --> 02:32:31.185
(ANTHONY LAUGHING)

02:32:38.152 --> 02:32:40.154
(ANTHONY EXCLAIMING)

02:32:45.479 --> 02:32:47.481
(ANTHONY CHATTERING)

02:32:57.692 --> 02:32:59.734
(BELL TOLLING)

02:35:05.862 --> 02:35:07.864
Mike, can I
have a minute?

02:35:18.355 --> 02:35:20.657
Barzini wants to
arrange a meeting.

02:35:20.757 --> 02:35:24.040
He says
we can straighten any
of our problems out.

02:35:24.721 --> 02:35:25.742
You talked to him?

02:35:25.842 --> 02:35:27.844
Yeah.

02:35:28.285 --> 02:35:32.049
I can arrange security.
On my territory.

02:35:35.172 --> 02:35:37.074
All right?

02:35:37.174 --> 02:35:38.755
All right.

02:35:38.855 --> 02:35:40.858
All right.

02:35:55.192 --> 02:35:57.595
Do you know
how they're going
to come at you?

02:36:00.758 --> 02:36:04.441
They're arranging
a meeting in Brooklyn.
Tessio's ground.

02:36:06.644 --> 02:36:08.646
Where I'll be safe.

02:36:20.618 --> 02:36:24.282
I always thought it
would have been Clemenza,
not Tessio.

02:36:24.382 --> 02:36:28.146
It's a smart move.
Tessio was always smarter.

02:36:30.388 --> 02:36:32.390
But I'm going to wait.

02:36:32.910 --> 02:36:34.912
After the baptism.

02:36:37.195 --> 02:36:40.739
I've decided
to be godfather
to Connie's baby.

02:36:40.839 --> 02:36:45.243
And then I'll meet
with Don Barzini
and Tattaglia.

02:36:46.604 --> 02:36:48.927
All the heads
of the five families.

02:36:52.811 --> 02:36:54.813
(ORGAN PLAYING)

02:36:57.535 --> 02:36:59.538
(BABY CRYING)

02:37:15.634 --> 02:37:17.636
(RECITING IN LATIN)

02:37:47.907 --> 02:37:50.189
(RECITING CONTINUES)

02:39:10.471 --> 02:39:13.374
PRIEST: (IN ENGLISH)
Michael, do you believe
in God, the Father almighty,

02:39:13.474 --> 02:39:15.536
Creator of Heaven and Earth?

02:39:15.636 --> 02:39:17.098
I do.

02:39:17.198 --> 02:39:20.341
PRIEST: Do you believe
in Jesus Christ,
His only Son, our Lord?

02:39:20.441 --> 02:39:21.422
MICHAEL: I do.

02:39:21.522 --> 02:39:23.424
Do you believe
in the Holy Ghost,

02:39:23.524 --> 02:39:25.546
the Holy
Catholic Church?

02:39:25.646 --> 02:39:26.948
I do.

02:39:27.048 --> 02:39:29.290
(RECITING CONTINUES
IN LATIN)

02:40:00.001 --> 02:40:01.543
(BABY CRYING)

02:40:01.643 --> 02:40:03.645
(RECITING CONTINUES)

02:40:32.554 --> 02:40:36.798
PRIEST: (IN ENGLISH)
Michael Francis Rizzi,
do you renounce Satan?

02:40:43.045 --> 02:40:45.047
I do renounce him.

02:40:54.296 --> 02:40:56.298
And all his works?

02:41:03.946 --> 02:41:05.948
(MUFFLED SHOUTING)

02:41:09.392 --> 02:41:11.394
I do renounce them.

02:41:12.154 --> 02:41:14.156
WOMAN: Oh, God!

02:41:16.319 --> 02:41:18.581
PRIEST:
And all his pomps?

02:41:18.681 --> 02:41:20.683
I do renounce them.

02:41:35.738 --> 02:41:40.003
Michael Rizzi,
will you be baptized?

02:41:40.103 --> 02:41:41.284
I will.

02:41:41.384 --> 02:41:43.386
(RECITING IN LATIN)

02:41:48.632 --> 02:41:51.334
(IN ENGLISH)
Michael Rizzi,
go in peace,

02:41:51.434 --> 02:41:54.418
and may the Lord
be with you. Amen.

02:41:54.518 --> 02:41:56.520
(CHURCH BELLS RINGING)

02:41:59.322 --> 02:42:01.324
(ALL CHATTERING)

02:42:08.251 --> 02:42:10.113
Kay!

02:42:10.213 --> 02:42:12.216
Kiss your godfather.

02:42:24.108 --> 02:42:26.110
(INAUDIBLE)

02:42:36.600 --> 02:42:40.665
Carlo, can't go to Vegas.
Something's come up.

02:42:40.765 --> 02:42:42.386
Everybody has to
leave without us.

02:42:42.486 --> 02:42:44.308
CONNIE: Oh, Mike,
it's our first vacation!

02:42:44.408 --> 02:42:45.870
Connie, please.

02:42:45.970 --> 02:42:48.472
Go back to the house,
wait for my call.
It's important.

02:42:48.572 --> 02:42:50.114
All right.

02:42:50.214 --> 02:42:52.577
I'll only be
a couple of days.

02:42:55.419 --> 02:42:57.421
(INDISTINCT CONVERSATION)

02:43:09.033 --> 02:43:11.276
We're on our way
to Brooklyn.

02:43:13.318 --> 02:43:15.740
I hope Mike can get us
a good deal tonight.

02:43:15.840 --> 02:43:17.842
I'm sure he will.

02:43:24.769 --> 02:43:30.195
Sal, Tom, the boss says
he'll come in a separate car,
so you two go on ahead.

02:43:30.295 --> 02:43:32.758
Hell, he can't do that.
It screws up all
my arrangements.

02:43:32.858 --> 02:43:34.079
Oh, that's what he said.

02:43:34.179 --> 02:43:36.181
I can't go either, Sal.

02:43:47.993 --> 02:43:52.037
Tell Mike
it was only business.
I always liked him.

02:43:53.759 --> 02:43:54.820
He understands that.

02:43:54.920 --> 02:43:56.922
Excuse me, Sal.

02:44:02.608 --> 02:44:05.050
Tom, can you get me
off the hook?

02:44:06.251 --> 02:44:07.553
For old times' sake?

02:44:07.653 --> 02:44:09.655
Can't do it, Sally.

02:44:41.087 --> 02:44:43.089
(TELEPHONE BEING DIALED)

02:44:54.701 --> 02:44:56.983
You have to answer
for Santino, Carlo.

02:45:02.429 --> 02:45:03.890
Mike, you got it
all wrong.

02:45:03.990 --> 02:45:07.294
You fingered Sonny
for Barzini.

02:45:07.394 --> 02:45:11.057
Ah, that little farce
you played
with my sister.

02:45:11.157 --> 02:45:12.979
You think that could fool
a Corleone?

02:45:13.079 --> 02:45:16.463
Mike, I'm innocent.
I swear on the kids, Mike.

02:45:16.563 --> 02:45:18.565
Please, Mike, don't do this.
Sit down.

02:45:21.928 --> 02:45:24.291
Don't do this
to me, please.

02:45:33.380 --> 02:45:35.382
Barzini is dead.

02:45:37.104 --> 02:45:39.186
So is Philip Tattaglia.

02:45:40.708 --> 02:45:42.710
Moe Greene.

02:45:43.390 --> 02:45:47.314
Strachi. Cuneo.

02:45:48.876 --> 02:45:50.618
Today I settle
all family business,

02:45:50.718 --> 02:45:54.221
so don't tell me
you're innocent, Carlo.

02:45:54.321 --> 02:45:56.323
Admit what you did.

02:45:59.967 --> 02:46:01.969
Get him a drink.

02:46:07.975 --> 02:46:09.977
Come on.

02:46:10.578 --> 02:46:12.960
Don't be afraid, Carlo.

02:46:13.060 --> 02:46:16.804
Come on. Do you think
I'd make my sister
a widow?

02:46:16.904 --> 02:46:19.707
I'm godfather
to your son, Carlo.

02:46:26.794 --> 02:46:28.836
Go ahead, drink, drink.

02:46:33.521 --> 02:46:38.346
No, Carlo, you're out
of the family business.
That's your punishment.

02:46:38.446 --> 02:46:42.470
You're finished.
I'm putting you on a plane
to Vegas.

02:46:42.570 --> 02:46:44.572
Tom.

02:46:48.336 --> 02:46:50.839
I want you to stay there.
Understand?

02:46:50.939 --> 02:46:52.040
Mmm-hmm.

02:46:52.140 --> 02:46:55.804
Only don't tell me
you're innocent.

02:46:55.904 --> 02:47:00.188
Because it insults
my intelligence.
Makes me very angry.

02:47:04.473 --> 02:47:06.515
Now, who approached you?

02:47:07.636 --> 02:47:10.038
Tattaglia or Barzini?

02:47:17.806 --> 02:47:19.808
It was Barzini.

02:47:23.692 --> 02:47:25.694
Good.

02:47:31.420 --> 02:47:35.444
There's a car
waiting outside to take
you to the airport.

02:47:35.544 --> 02:47:38.227
I'll call your wife
and tell her
what flight you're on.

02:47:43.432 --> 02:47:45.995
Mike...
Come on, get out of my sight.

02:48:12.021 --> 02:48:14.023
Hello, Carlo.

02:48:17.067 --> 02:48:19.069
(GRUNTING)

02:49:12.002 --> 02:49:13.184
(CONNIE SCREAMING)

02:49:13.284 --> 02:49:14.505
I'm trying
to tell you...

02:49:14.605 --> 02:49:16.847
CONNIE: Oh, Mama, please!

02:49:22.213 --> 02:49:24.215
(SOBBING)

02:49:25.016 --> 02:49:27.078
Michael! Michael!

02:49:27.178 --> 02:49:29.420
KAY: What is it?
CONNIE: Where is he? Michael!

02:49:31.863 --> 02:49:36.688
Michael, you lousy bastard!
You killed my husband.

02:49:36.788 --> 02:49:40.932
You waited until Papa died,
so nobody could stop you
and then you killed him.

02:49:41.032 --> 02:49:44.255
You blamed him for Sonny.
You always did. Everybody did.

02:49:44.355 --> 02:49:47.859
But you never thought
about me! You never gave
a damn about me!

02:49:47.959 --> 02:49:49.941
Now what are we gonna do?

02:49:50.041 --> 02:49:52.043
KAY: Connie.

02:49:54.085 --> 02:49:56.708
CONNIE: Why do you think
he kept Carlo at the Mall?

02:49:56.808 --> 02:49:59.551
All the time he knew
he was going to kill him.

02:49:59.651 --> 02:50:02.394
And you stood godfather
to our baby.

02:50:02.494 --> 02:50:04.956
You lousy
cold-hearted bastard!

02:50:05.056 --> 02:50:07.479
Want to know how many men
he had killed with Carlo?

02:50:07.579 --> 02:50:09.201
Read the papers,
read the papers!

02:50:09.301 --> 02:50:12.144
That's your husband,
that's your husband!

02:50:14.186 --> 02:50:16.188
(CONNIE SPITTING)

02:50:19.591 --> 02:50:21.653
(CONNIE SOBBING)

02:50:21.753 --> 02:50:25.898
No! No, no...

02:50:25.998 --> 02:50:29.361
Take her upstairs.
Get her a doctor.

02:50:33.245 --> 02:50:35.247
(MICHAEL SIGHS)

02:50:50.262 --> 02:50:52.264
She's hysterical.

02:50:56.749 --> 02:50:58.751
Hysterical.

02:51:00.433 --> 02:51:02.435
Michael, is it true?

02:51:04.116 --> 02:51:06.179
Don't ask me
about my business, Kay.

02:51:06.279 --> 02:51:07.900
Is it true?

02:51:08.000 --> 02:51:09.542
Don't ask me
about my business.

02:51:09.642 --> 02:51:11.644
No.
Enough!

02:51:30.824 --> 02:51:32.826
All right.

02:51:35.148 --> 02:51:37.150
This one time.

02:51:41.074 --> 02:51:43.276
This one time
I'll let you ask me
about my affairs.

02:51:50.323 --> 02:51:52.325
Is it true?

02:51:55.809 --> 02:51:57.811
Is it?

02:51:58.812 --> 02:52:00.814
No.

02:52:14.428 --> 02:52:17.471
I guess
we both need a drink.
Come on.

02:52:29.603 --> 02:52:31.605
(GLASS CLINKING)

02:52:48.503 --> 02:52:50.505
Don Corleone.
